X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre": "https://jccc.on.ca/event/2026/11/aki-no-tabi"}
X-SOURCE-ID:jccc
SUMMARY:Aki no Tabi | 秋の旅
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T190000
UID:1e43949a1b1cd702dee939d13411dc35@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:Aki no Tabi — Autumn at the JCCC This fall\, join us at the 
 JCCC for a new seasonal experience celebrating Japanese and Japanese Canad
 ian culture through creativity\, connection\, and hands-on activities. Ins
 pired by the nostalgic charm of Japan and the cozy feeling of autumn trans
 itioning into winter\, Aki no Tabi is a place to slow down\, create\, conn
 ect\, and enjoy the season together. Come experience the warmth and nostal
 gia of autumn at the JCCC. 🍂 Event Map Pet Policy For the comfort and s
 afety of all guests\, no pets are allowed at the event with the exception 
 of service animals. We appreciate your cooperation and look forward to see
 ing you at Aki no Tabi! Schedule Ongoing Activities (1pm-7pm) Paradise Exh
 ibition Autumn Market (Marketplace Vendors) Artisans' Town (Hands-on Activ
 ity Area) Feast Alley (JCCC Food & Food Vendors) Story Alley (JCCC Library
  & Book Sale) 1:00 pm - 7:00 pm Time Specific Events Live Music by Spare B
 edroom Main Entrance 2:30 pm - 4:00 pm A.S.M. Kobayashi Artist Talk Herita
 ge Court 3:00 pm - 4:00 pm Live Music by Spare Bedroom Main Entrance 5:00 
 pm - 6:30 pm Workshops (Tickets on Sale!) Journaling & Paper Craft - Craft
 ing Our Narratives with Erica H. Isomura and Nico Koyanagi Sakura Room 1:3
 0 pm - 4:00 pm Ceramics - Autumn Leaves Mamezara with Secret Teatime Herit
 age Lounge 1:30 pm - 3:00 pm Crochet - Make Your Own Amigurumi with So Cra
 ftful MNHC Museum 1:00 pm - 3:00 pm Wagashi Making - Enjoy Daifuku with At
 elier Wa Wynford Room 2:00 pm - 3:30 pm Ceramics - Autumn Leaves Mamezara 
 with Secret Teatime Heritage Lounge 4:00 pm - 5:30 pm Crochet - Make Your 
 Own Amigurumi with So Craftful MNHC Museum 3:30 pm - 5:30 pm Wagashi Makin
 g - Enjoy Daifuku with Atelier Wa Wynford Room 4:30 pm - 6:00 pm Autumn Ma
 rket Marketplace Vendors Feast Alley JCCC Food & Food Vendors Artisans' To
 wn Hands-on Activity Vendors Create a cute fruit parfait photo and memo ho
 lder with air-dry clay. A fun 30-minute activity for all ages. Fee: $10 Ma
 ke a mini wreath or bouquet necklace. Add lava stones for essential oils o
 r dried flowers for a personal touch. Fee: $20 Explore ceramic fracture pa
 tterns and transfer your favorite design onto a pendant to create a unique
  kintsugi keepsake. Fee: $30 (Chain sold separately) A beautiful mix of ha
 nd-selected succulents\, each featuring unique shapes\, textures\, and col
 ours. A lovely\, low-maintenance addition to any home or a thoughtful gift
  for someone special. Fee: $19.99 Explore tarot for guidance and inspirati
 on or try your luck with a traditional Japanese omikuji fortune slip. Taro
 t Readings: $10-$58 Omikuji: $2 Discover 19th-century rug hooking and quil
 ting with costumed interpreters\, then create your own quilt square to tak
 e home. Fee: By donation Design a button badge featuring historic photos f
 rom the JCCC Archives. Meet our team and discover how we preserve Japanese
  Canadian heritage. Fee: By donation Create your own keychain or water bot
 tle holder using paracord. Choose from a variety of colours\, patterns\, a
 nd charms to make it your own. Fee: $12-15 A.S.M. Kobayashi Artist Talk Jo
 in award-winning interdisciplinary artist A.S.M. Kobayashi for an engaging
  talk exploring her creative practice through found recordings\, everyday 
 objects\, performance\, and storytelling. Discover her 20-year artistic jo
 urney\, including her acclaimed performance Say Something Bunny!\, and her
  latest work\, Electric Neon Clock\, which transforms her family's WWII in
 ternment records into an immersive installation combining archival materia
 ls\, video\, sound\, and performance. A.S.M. Kobayashi Based in Toronto an
 d NYC\, A.S.M. Kobayashi is an internationally recognized artist working a
 cross performance\, video\, installation\, and illustration. She is a Crea
 tive Capital Awardee and a fellow of Yaddo and MacDowell. Her solo exhibit
 ion\, Electric Neon Clock\, is on view at the Art Gallery of Mississauga u
 ntil October 25\, with live performances from October 21–24.\n\nCategori
 es: Community Event\, Social
LOCATION:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
URL:https://jccc.on.ca/event/2026/11/aki-no-tabi
X-SOURCE:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
END:VEVENT
