CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Co-op &amp\; Career Centre,Colleges,Division
 s and Special Areas,Faculties,Faculty of Environmental &amp\; Urban Change
 ,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Programs),Facult
 y of Liberal Arts &amp\; Professional Studies,Faculty of Science,Future St
 udents,Glendon,Glendon Research,Graduate Program in Biology,Graduate Progr
 am in Disaster &amp\; Emergency Management,Graduate Program in Earth &amp\
 ; Space Science,Graduate Program in Electrical Engineering &amp\; Computer
  Science,Graduate Program in Environmental Studies,Graduate Program in Geo
 graphy,Graduate Program in Information Systems &amp\; Technology,Graduate 
 Program in Interdisciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in Science &amp\; Te
 chnology Studies,LA&amp\;PS Alumni,LA&amp\;PS Colleges,LA&amp\;PS Future S
 tudents,LA&amp\;PS Open to the Public,LA&amp\;PS School of Administrative 
 Studies,LA&amp\;PS Students All,LA&amp\;PS Students-Graduate,LA&amp\;PS St
 udents-International,LA&amp\;PS Students-Undergrad,Lassonde School of Engi
 neering,ORUs,Regional Alumni Events,Research &amp\; Innovation,Students,th
 e Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students,YFile newsletter
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261109
DESCRIPTION:This course aims to give participants a thorough understanding
  of multispectral mapping and its drone applications. Combining classroom 
 instruction\, hands-on drone flying\, and practical image analysis\, it pr
 epares learners to plan and execute multispectral surveys\, gather quality
  data\, and analyze multispectral images for real-world uses. By course en
 d\, participants will acquire both theoretical knowledge and practical ski
 lls applicable to sectors like agriculture\, environmental monitoring\, fo
 restry\, water resource management\, and disaster risk reduction.\nA micro
 credit certificate will be issued to all participants from CIFAL York upon
  completion of the course.\nCourse Details:\n👥 Eligibility: Open to eve
 ryone (no prior mapping experience required).\n🗓️ Date: Saturday\, No
 vember 14\, 2026\n⏰ Time: Full-day intensive session (9:00 AM – 5:30 P
 M).\n📍 Location: ADERSIM Lab\, Schulich Building (N004)\, York Universi
 ty\, Toronto\n🎓 Student Perk: 50% DISCOUNT for full-time students\n⚠
 ️ Seats are limited to ensure all participants receive dedicated flight 
 practice time\n🔗 Registration and More Info: https://lnkd.in/gGds4exr\n
 ⏳ Registration closes Thursday\, November 12.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109
LOCATION:Room N004 Schulich School of Business Building (Basement Floor)
ORGANIZER;CN="CIFAL York":MAILTO:cifalpresident@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
