SUMMARY: Lemons Lemons Lemons Lemons Lemons
DESCRIPTION:What would you say if you had only 140 words a day?\n\nDiscov
 er Sam Steiner's play this November.\n\nPresented at The Assembly Theatre
  in November 2026\, Lemons Lemons Lemons Lemons Lemons is part rom-com\, 
 part sci-fi\, and part dystopian drama.\n\nThe average person will speak 
 123\,205\,750 words in a lifetime. But what if there were a limit? Oliver
  and Bernadette are about to find out. Lemons Lemons Lemons Lemons Lemons
  imagines a world where we’re forced to say less. It’s about what we say 
 and how we say it\; about the things we can only hear in the silence\; ab
 out dead cats\, activism\, eye contact and lemons\, lemons\, lemons\, lem
 ons\, lemons.\n\nDirected by Bonnie Duff (Assistant Director Jane Austen’
 s Northanger Abbey\, Guild Festival Theatre\; Playwright/Performer This F
 eels Like The End\, Theatre Aurinko/Next Stage Festival) and starring Lar
 a Lucia (The Drowsy Chaperone\, Shifting Ground Collective\; Brontë: The 
 World Without\, Guild Festival Theatre) and Jack Copland (The Moors\, Rio
 t King Theatre\; The Comeback\, Globus Theatre)\, Lemons Lemons Lemons Le
 mons Lemons features Scenic Design by Kenzia Dalie (Panoply Collective\; 
 Full House Productions)\, Lighting Design by Jay Hines (Crow’s Theatre\; 
 Shifting Ground Collective)\, and Sound Design by Jake Schindler (Mixtape
  Productions\; Second City\; Stratford Festival).\n\nDirected by Bonnie D
 uff\n\nProduced by Bonnie Duff and Miranda Wiseman\n\nFeaturing Lara Luci
 a as Bernadette and Jack Copland as Oliver\n\nScenic Design by Kenzia Dal
 ie\n\nSound Design by Jake Schindler\n\nLighting Design by Jay Hines\n\nP
 roduction Managed by Jeremy Hutton\n\n\nTICKETS*\n\nArts Worker / Student
  / Senior General Admission: $25\n\nAdult General Admission: $30\n\nLEMON
 S Supporter General Admission: $35\n\n(Plus fees)\n\nPresented at The Ass
 embly Theatre (1479 Queen St W\, Toronto\, ON M6R 1A1)\, November 6th-15t
 h 2026\n\nFriday November 6th - 8:00 (Opening Night)\n\nSaturday November
  7th - 8:00\n\nSunday November 8th - 5:00pm & 8:00pm\n\nTuesday November 
 10th - 8:00pm\n\nWednesday November 11th - 8:00pm\n\nThursday November 12
 th - 8:00pm\n\nFriday November 13th - 8:00pm\n\nSaturday November 14th - 
 5:00pm & 8:00pm\n\nSunday November 15th - 12:00pm
CATEGORIES:Dance---Performance---Theatre,The-Assembly-Theatre
