UID:147288-1794850200-1794861000@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Empty Bowls
DESCRIPTION:Empty Bowls            \n                                    \n                                \n                        \n                                                \n                                                        Get Tickets                        \n                                            \n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Monday November 16\, 2026\n5:30 pm – 8:30 pm\nTicket holders can line up starting at 4:30 pm\nRemarks at 6:30 pm \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Please Note: While tickets are sold out\, you can still make a difference. Anishnawbe Health Foundation is accepting donations in support of Indigenous-led healthcare and the vital programs and services offered by Anishnawbe Health Toronto. Click here to support Anishnawbe Health Foundation with a donation. \nJoin us for our annual Empty Bowls fundraising event in support of Anishnawbe Health Foundation (AHF)\, a registered charity that works with generous donors to help improve the health and wellness of Toronto’s Indigenous community. \nSelect a handcrafted ceramic bowl\, donated by a local potter and sample a selection of delicious soups prepared by top local chefs\, as well as cornbread made by Chef Bianca Azupardo of Clay Restaurant. Take your bowl home at the end of the evening as a keepsake. \nWe extend our heartfelt thanks to everyone whose contributions make this event possible\, including the chefs\, potters\, volunteers\, and attendees. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nSold Out \n\n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Tickets : $100\n                                        \n                      \n\n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n              \n                        \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information \n\nEntry is on a first-come\, first-served basis\nTicket holders can line up starting at 4:30 pm. The ticket holder line will begin in the lobby of the Museum and continue outside onto the Gardiner Plaza. The line will start entering at 5:30 pm. Please dress appropriately for the weather\nThis event is standing room with very limited seating. If you require accommodations\, please note them at checkout\n\nPlease Note: The Gardiner Museum does not issue tax receipts for tickets purchased for Empty Bowls. All proceeds are donated directly to Anishnawbe Health Foundation (AHF). Additional donations to Anishnawbe Health Foundation (AHF) can be made through their website. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Anishnawbe Health Foundation (AHF) \nThanks to donor support\, Anishnawbe Health Foundation (AHF) helps create an environment where the urban Indigenous community can heal spiritually\, physically\, emotionally\, and mentally. They do this by enhancing capital and program funding for Anishnawbe Health Toronto (AHT)\, and by supporting the reclamation\, preservation\, research\, and sharing of traditional healing methods with all people. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Participating Chefs and Restaurants \nAdam Lafleur\, Constantine Restaurant\nBianca Azupardo\, Clay Restaurant\nDacyion Reid\, Dacy’s Gourmet Kitchen\nDonna Dooher\, Mildred’s Temple Kitchen\nNabil Dahmani\, Louf Restaurant\nJoseph Shawana\, Niichii’s Street Eats\nKeith Hoare\, Thistletown Collegiate Institute\nLorenzo Loseto\, GEORGE Restaurant\nPriyantha Batepola\, PRI’S SMOKE BBQ\nTulio Lessa\, Centennial College \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Thank you to the following potters for donating bowls: \nAimee Hawkins\, Ana Antunez Dominguez\, Andrea Liao\, Annika Hoefs\, Arlene Kushnir\, Asa Meyer\, Atsuko Kobasigawa\, Audrey Mah\, Brenda Nieves\, Bruce Taylor\, Deborah Schippling\, Dominique Nanoff\, Elisabeth Kalbuss\, Florence Ngan\, Gwen Friedman\, Juana Berinstein\, Kapri Rabin\, Karen Franzen\, Katie Argyle\, Kerri Jerome\, Lana Rayman\, Marla Benton\, Mary Goh\, Mary McKenzie\, Minda Davis\, Natasha Martin\, Noel Yardley\, Scott Barnim\, Sequoia Miller\, Susan Collett\, Talia Silva\, Taylor Hogan\, Teresa Dunlop\, Thomas Aitken & Kate Hyde\, Valentina Guevara\, Veronika von Nostiza-Tait \nSpecial thanks to:\n \nFUSION Clay and Glass Association\nHill Potters Guild\nIngersoll Creative Arts Centre\nMississauga Potters’ Guild\nSheridan College Craft and Design\, Ceramics\nThe Potter’s Studio Inc\nToronto Potters \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n              \n                    \n                In Partnership With\n                \n                                \n                            \n                    \n                Cornbread Donated By\n                \n                                \n                            \n            \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          \n                    \n          \n            \n                          \n          \n        \n\n      \n        \n          \n                    \n          \n            \n                          \n          \n        \n\n      \n        \n          \n                    \n          \n            \n                          \n          \n        \n\n      \n        \n          \n                    \n          \n            \n                          \n          \n        \n\n      \n        \n          \n                    \n          \n            \n                          \n          \n        \n\n      \n        \n          \n                    \n          \n            \n                          \n          \n        \n\n      \n        \n          \n                    \n          \n            \n                          \n          \n        \n\n      \n        \n          \n                    \n          \n            \n                          \n          \n        \n\n          \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/empty-bowls-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Programs & Events
