SUMMARY:Macrame a Christmas Tree with 3D Printed Parts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T190000
UID:6adfe2d7ad40276591551f7b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Explore one of the possibilities of 3D printings in your daily
  life!\nIn this in-person program\, you will learn how to make a Keychain 
 or bracelet for yourself by combining traditional macramé braiding skill
 s with new technology 3D design and printing.\nThis is an in-person event\
 , registration required via Eventbrite two weeks before. Each child 6-12 y
 ears old should accompany an adult. For safety reason\, no child under 6 
 years old allowed in this program.\nLimited drop-in spots available.\nPlea
 se be noted that your spot will be taken by others if you failed to show u
 p 5 mins after class begins.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal
  information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under
  the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inform
 ation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and 
 evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can b
 e directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 78
 9 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, 3rd floor\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6adfe2d7ad40276591551f7b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
