X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Make A Will with the Ontario Bar Association
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T113000
UID:6ada2de896ec3a003adc3840@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November is Make a Will Month and TPL is delighted to host the
  Ontario Bar Association. Learn about the importance of having a will and 
 powers of attorney for you and your family. Matias Gutierrez\, a member o
 f the\nOntario Bar Association\nwho practices Trusts and Estates Law will 
 speak about the elements of a will\, what happens if you don’t have one\
 , what are powers of attorney\, why they are important and special conside
 rations to keep in mind when preparing your estate and care plans. Note\, 
 this program is for general information only\, not for drafting individual
  wills.
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Room 204
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ada2de896ec3a003adc3840
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
