SUMMARY:Blatant Injustice The Internment of Jewish Refugees in Canada duri
 ng World War II
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T193000
UID:6a8f51104cb69d003e2398cf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Journalist and editor Ian Darragh discusses the harrowing expe
 riences of Jewish refugees to Canada\, who were treated as enemies and imp
 risoned in internment camps during World War II. Yet the internees\, who w
 ere Holocaust survivors\, did not let the authorities crush their spirit. 
 Walter Igersheimer's Blatant Injustice is a story of resilience and deter
 mination.\nBlatant Injustice by Walter W. Igersheimer\, edited by Ian Darr
 agh
LOCATION:Yorkville\, Main floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f51104cb69d003e2398cf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
