 cessibility (CCC),Equity, Diversity &amp\; Inclusion,Equity, People &amp\;
  Culture,Faculties,Faculty of Education,Faculty of Environmental &amp\; Ur
 ban Change,Faculty of Health,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp\; Professional S
 tudies,Faculty of Science,FSc AIPHA,FSc Biology,FSc Chemistry,FSc Division
  of Natural Science,FSc LIAM,FSc Mathematics &amp\; Statistics,FSc Physics
  &amp\; Astronomy,FSc Science, Technology &amp\; Society,Graduate Program 
 in Global Health,Health Education &amp\; Promotion,LA&amp\;PS Colleges,LA&
 amp\;PS Community Hub,LA&amp\;PS Department of Anthropology,LA&amp\;PS Dep
 artment of Communication &amp\; Media Studies,LA&amp\;PS Department of Eco
 nomics,LA&amp\;PS Department of English,LA&amp\;PS Department of Equity St
 udies,LA&amp\;PS Department of French Studies,LA&amp\;PS Department of His
 tory,LA&amp\;PS Department of Humanities,LA&amp\;PS Department of Language
 s, Literatures &amp\; Linguistics,LA&amp\;PS Department of Philosophy,LA&a
 mp\;PS Department of Politics,LA&amp\;PS Department of Social Science,LA&a
 mp\;PS Department of Sociology,LA&amp\;PS Employee Research Workshops,LA&a
 mp\;PS ESLOLC,LA&amp\;PS Founders College,LA&amp\;PS Future Students,LA&am
 p\;PS Internship Information Sessions,LA&amp\;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp
 \;PS Multimedia Language Centre,LA&amp\;PS Nellie Library,LA&amp\;PS New C
 ollege,LA&amp\;PS School of Administrative Studies,LA&amp\;PS School of Ge
 nder, Sexuality and Women's Studies,LA&amp\;PS School of Human Resources M
 anagement,LA&amp\;PS School of Information Technology,LA&amp\;PS School of
  Public Policy &amp\; Administration,LA&amp\;PS School of Social Work,LA&a
 mp\;PS SCOLAPS,LA&amp\;PS SNACK,LA&amp\;PS Student Success,LA&amp\;PS Stud
 ents All,LA&amp\;PS Students-Graduate,LA&amp\;PS Students-International,LA
 &amp\;PS Students-Undergrad,LA&amp\;PS Vanier College,LA&amp\;PS Vanier Co
 llege Productions,Stong College,Student Counselling, Health &amp\; Well-be
 ing,Students,Well-being
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261109
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever felt like the places that shaped you\, whether n
 earby or far across the world\, are changing?\nA World Café: Conversation
 s on Climate Change and Belonging is a space to reflect\, share\, and con
 nect through guided conversations about how environmental change impacts o
 ur sense of identity\, memory\, and the idea of home.\nTogether\, we will 
 explore how climate change affects our emotional lives and sense of belong
 ing\, while creating space for connection\, community\, and hope. Whether 
 you are thinking about places like Sudan\, the Philippines\, the Caribbean
 \, Bangladesh\, Syria\, or right here in Toronto\, your experiences are we
 lcome.\nYou do not need to be an expert to join. This is a space for emoti
 onal honesty\, shared reflection\, and meaningful conversation.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109
LOCATION:101 Stong (MDR)
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/a-world-cafe-conversations-on-climate-c
 hange-and-belonging-3/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
