SUMMARY:[In]Security: Military Portraiture of Gertrude Kearns
DTSTART:20261118T173000Z
DTEND:20261211T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20261111T210900Z
UID:MEC-29093d10b0c57f776c78f839d0203739@events.yorku.ca__20261118
SEQUENCE:4
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 11/ARTH4110-Poster_Page_2-1-scaled.jpg
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Bethune College,Calumet College,Colleges,Div
 isions and Special Areas,Equity, Diversity &amp\; Inclusion,Equity, People
  &amp\; Culture,Faculties,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Graduate Program in 
 Art History,Graduate Program in Visual Art,Recruitment,Regional Alumni Eve
 nts,Stong College,Students,YFile newsletter
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261111
DESCRIPTION:[In] Security\, evokes the tensions between protection and vul
 nerability\, certainty and instability. Made between 2002 and 2026\, these
  works are portraits of real people: Canadian Armed Forces senior officers
  at critical moments in Canada’s military history. They are also records
  of the systems around them. Uniforms\, maps\, borders\, slogans\, insigni
 a and military jargon move the image beyond likeness\, locating the indivi
 dual within larger structures of geography\, conflict and institutional po
 wer.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261111
LOCATION:Joan Goldfarb Study Centre\, 275 Joan &amp\; Martin Goldfarb Cent
 re for Fine Arts @ 86 Fine Arts Road\, Toronto
ORGANIZER;CN="Department of Visual Art and Art History":MAILTO:
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/insecurity-military-portraiture-of-gert
 rude-kearns-2/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/graduate-faculty-meet-up/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Graduate Faculty Meet Up
DTSTART:20261118T173000Z
DTEND:20261118T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T040100Z
UID:MEC-9c87b4fa747d4b5675c82f561eb9cd4c@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261118T173000Z
SEQUENCE:3
CATEGORIES:Faculty Affairs,Faculty of Graduate Studies
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261029
DESCRIPTION:\nThe Office of the Vice-Provost Faculty and the Faculty of Gr
 aduate Studies invite you to join us for the online Fall 2026 Graduate Fac
 ulty Meet-Up on Wednesday\, November 18\, 2026.\nWhether you are new to g
 raduate supervision or looking to exchange ideas with colleagues\, this se
 ssion offers an opportunity to learn\, connect\, and share experiences in 
 a supportive setting.\n\n\n\nThis online graduate faculty meet up invites 
 seasoned and new graduate faculty members to share practical insights on 
 graduate supervision\, including fostering work-life balance while teachin
 g\, researching and supervising graduate students. To open the meet up\, w
 e have planned a panel discussion of experienced graduate supervisors f
 ollowed by an opportunity to continue the conversation in breakout rooms a
 nd connect with colleagues from across the University.\n\n\n\nDate: Wedne
 sday\, November 18\, 2026Time: 12:30 p.m. – 2:00 p.m. (ET)Location: On
 line via ZoomRegistration: Click to Register\n\n\n\nGraduate Faculty Pane
 lists\n\n\n\n\nDr. Garrett Melenka\, Associate Professor\, Lassonde School
  of Engineering \n\n\n\nDr. Alison Bain\, Professor\, Faculty of Environm
 ental and Urban Change\n\n\n\nDr. Cindel White\, Assistant Professor\, Dep
 t of Psychology\n\n\n\nDr. Trevor VandenBoer\, Assistant Professor\, Dept 
 of Chemistry\n\n\n\n\nDiscussion Topics\n\n\n\n\nGraduate supervision tips
  and tricks\n\n\n\nMaintaining work-life balance\n\n\n\nAdvice from experi
 enced graduate faculty members\n\n\n\nInteractive breakout room discussion
 s and networking\n\n\n\n\nBring your lunch to this virtual gathering and
  join the conversation!\n\n\n\nFor more information\, contact Tracy Bhoola
  ( mailto:tbhoola@yorku.ca )\, Manager\, Graduate Supervision Support\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261029
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/graduate-faculty-meet-up/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
