BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre": "https://jccc.on.ca/event/ishizue-award-dinner-2026"}
X-SOURCE-ID:jccc
SUMMARY:The Ishizue Award Dinner 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T210000
UID:347d8d1f18cfb5c9917f91900a7007a9@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:The JCCC Board of Directors is pleased to announce that the 8t
 h Ishizue Award and accompanying dinner will be held on Thursday November 
 19\, 2026. The Ishizue Award acknowledges and expresses our appreciation a
 nd respect to members or friends who have made exceptional contributions t
 o the Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre. The name Ishizue\, meaning corner
 stone or foundation\, pays tribute to the 75 families who\, at significant
  personal financial risk\, guaranteed the original mortgage on the JCCC at
  123 Wynford Drive in the early 1960’s. These families provided the foun
 dation upon which the JCCC was built\, and their support for the JCCC will
  forever be recognized as the cornerstone for who we are as a community. T
 he recipients of this annual award are a very distinguished group of peopl
 e who have each made significant life contributions to the Japanese Canadi
 an Cultural Centre. They are: Ken Fukushima: Long time Judo program sensei
  since 1995 now retired Harry Kawabe: Entertainer from 1970’s at JCCC Ca
 ravan and head of clubs such as ukulele and now promotes programming for t
 he Japanese Seniors Akiko Maruoka: Japanese language head instructor since
  the 60’s Dave Ohashi (posthumous): Photographer and technical support a
 t events for over 40 years Connie Sugiyama: Past JCCC Board member and cur
 rent Advisor. Founder of Building Together Campaign\, Crane Tribute and th
 e Sedai Project David Tsubouchi : Past JCCC Board member from the 80’s\,
  chaired the Antique Road show\, a Cabinet Minister and helped strengthen 
 the JCCC and also Sakura Gala Chair over many years. We cordially invite y
 ou to honour these distinguished award recipients at an intimate and elega
 nt dinner on Thursday November 19th at 6:30pm at the Japanese Canadian Cul
 tural Centre. Black tie optional. Tickets are $180 each (plus HST) . Maxim
 um of 10 guests per table. To purchase tickets please order through the bu
 tton below or in person at the JCCC\, starting September 21\, 2026\, and e
 nding November 9\, 2026. Please contact Sharon Marubashi for any further i
 nformation by email or phone (647-291-4751). On behalf of all of the direc
 tors of the Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre\, we look forward to spendin
 g a special evening of recognition and celebration together. Agenda Cockta
 ils Dinner Evening's Greetings Catering by Spectrum Catering Entertainment
  Koto Performance by Aiko Fujii Greetings from JCCC President Chris Hope A
 ward Ceremony Group Photo Closing Remarks Aiko Fujii Aiko Fujii started le
 arning at the Ikuta School of Koto and Jiuta Shamisen at an early age. She
  is a licensed teacher at Kyoto Todokai School of Koto and Shamisen. In ad
 dition to performing\, she is actively involved in cross-genre collaborati
 ons and teaching.\n\nCategories: Community Event\, Social
LOCATION:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
URL:https://jccc.on.ca/event/ishizue-award-dinner-2026
X-SOURCE:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
END:VEVENT
