X-SOURCE-URLS:{"UofT Philosophy": "https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/eastern-study-group-of-the-north-american-kant-society/", "University of Toronto": "https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/eastern-study-group-of-the-north-american-kant-society/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Philosophy": "https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/eastern-study-group-of-the-north-american-kant-society/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:philosophy
X-SOURCE:University of Toronto, UofT Philosophy
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTSTAMP:20261111T150627Z
CREATED:20260910T170028Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261111T150627Z
UID:35761-1795132800-1795305599@philosophy.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:Eastern Study Group of the North American Kant Society
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the two-day meeting of the North American Kant Society Eastern Study Group. \nDAY 1: Friday\, November 20 – Room 100  \n\n\n\n9:30 AM – 10:30 AM\nPractical Philosophy\n“Kant’s Purely Practical Concept of Freedom”\nNoa Buckle (Toronto)\n*Nominated for Markus Herz Award*\n\n\n10:40 AM – 12:10 PM\nPractical Philosophy\n“Is there a Right to Visit? Juridical Community\, Spatial Fragmentation and Communication in Towards Perpetual Peace”\nAlice Pinheiro Walla (McMaster)\n\n\n 12:10 PM – 2:00 PM\nLunch Break\n\n\n2:00 PM – 3:30 PM\nMetaphysics\n“Kant’s Possibility Proof and the Myth of the ‘Metaphysical Kant'”\nMaya Krishnan (Chicago)\n\n\n3:40 PM – 5:10 PM\nMetaphysics\n“Analogical Grounding: Kant on the Relation between Phenomena and Noumena”\nLorenzo Spagnesi (Trier)\n\n\n5:30 Pm – 7:30 PM\n Keynote Address\n“The Juridical Interpretation of the Transcendental Deduction”\nArthur Ripstein (Toronto)\n\n\n\nDAY 2: Saturday\, November 21 – Room 100  \n\n\n\n9:30 AM – 10:30 AM\nThe Possibility of Cognition\n“Schematism\, Homogeneity\, and a Third Thing”\nFearghus Horan (Johns Hopkins University)\n*Nominated for Markus Herz Award and winner of the graduate travel stipend \n\n\n10:40 AM – 12:10 PM\nThe Possibility of Cognition\n“Humility and Relationality”\nDai Heide (Simon Fraser)\n\n\n 12:10 PM – 2:00 PM\nLunch Break\n\n\n2:00 PM – 3:30 PM\nJudgement\n“The Dilemma of Existential Judgments”\nMario Schärli (HU-Berlin)\n\n\n3:40 PM – 5:10 PM\nJudgement\n“Kant on Truth”\nAlexandra Newton (UC-Riverside)\n\n\n5:30 Pm – 7:30 PM\n Keynote Address\n“Kant and Schopenhauer on Practical Cognition of Things in Themselves”\nAnja Jauernig (NYU)\n\n\n\nDownload the schedule.
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/eastern-study-group-of-the-north-american-kant-society/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building 100
CATEGORIES:Graduate,St. George
ORGANIZER;CN="Nick Stang":MAILTO:nick.stang@utoronto.ca
END:VEVENT
