DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T153000
UID:6aebb53ffb96d55bb888d289@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on\nFriday\, November 20th\nat College/Shaw Library\nf
 or a mid-afternoon\nPA Day screening\nof Cartoon Network's first ever an
 imated mini-series\,\nOver the Garden Wall\n\, created by Patrick McHale\
 , one of the many brilliant minds behind Adventure Time. The series foll
 ows the story of two brothers\, Greg and Wirt\, who find themselves in a s
 trange forest. Along the way\, they meet a bluebird named Beatrice who hel
 ps them navigate the strange land in the hopes of making their way home. 
 This program will take place between\n1:30-3:30pm\nin the downstairs Aud
 itorium for\nchildren ages 0-12\nand their parents\, guardians\, and/or c
 aregivers.\nD\nrop-in\, no registration required\nIf you or your child liv
 es with a disability\, and requires an accessibility accommodation to part
 icipate in this program\, please contact Accessibility Services by email\n
 accessibleservices@tpl.ca\nor voicemail\, 416-393-7099\, to make a request
 . Please contact at least three weeks in advance.
LOCATION:College/Shaw\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aebb53ffb96d55bb888d289
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
