SUMMARY:PA Day: Relay Education STEM Workshop: Capture the Wind
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T150000
UID:6ad918b59d27a000455272a5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Spend your PA Day afternoon at Bendale library! Capture the W
 ind is a curriculum-linked workshop\, which examines electricity\, circuit
 s\, and renewable energy\, and specifically focuses on wind power. Partici
 pants will learn how wind energy can be harnessed for electricity and will
  discover through experiments why wind turbines are designed with certain 
 components in mind.\nAges 8-12\, Space is limited.\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles
  your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Bendale\, Lower Level\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad918b59d27a000455272a5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
