CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp\; Urban Change,Faculty of Health,
 Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp\; Professional Studies,Faculty of Science,Las
 sonde School of Engineering,ORUs,Osgoode Hall Law School,Y-EMERGE
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261112
DESCRIPTION:Are you\, or someone you know\, interested in floods\, wildfir
 es\, climate change\, emergency response\, technology such as VR and drone
 s\, public safety\, or helping communities prepare for\, respond to and re
 cover from disasters?\nJoin us for Disaster Day 2026 a free interactive ev
 ent designed specifically for high school students\, young adults\, and th
 ose curious about the exciting world of disaster and emergency management 
 as well as research on crises and disasters. Learn about disaster-related 
 studies at York University\, including connections to many disciplines suc
 h as health\, engineering\, law\, public administration\, sociology\, etc.
 \n📅 Date: Saturday\, November 21\, 2026\n🕐 Time: 1:00 p.m. to 4:00 p
 .m.\n📍 Location: York University\, Keele Campus (exact location will be
  shared upon registration)\nThrough hands-on activities\, demonstrations\,
  and conversations with professionals and researchers\, participants will 
 discover how communities prepare for\, respond to\, and recover from disas
 ters.\nEvent Highlights\n🔥 Wildfire Community Challenge Work together a
 s part of an emergency management team to protect a community during a sim
 ulated wildfire scenario. Explore the decisions emergency managers must ma
 ke under pressure and see how collaboration can save lives and reduce impa
 cts.\n🚁 Virtual Reality and Drone Demonstrations See how cutting-edge t
 echnologies are used to assess damage\, monitor hazards\, support emergenc
 y response\, and help communities reduce disaster risk.\n🌪️ How Scien
 tists Predict and Communicate Risk Learn how mathematicians\, emergency ma
 nagers\, and researchers use science to predict and communicate hazard imp
 acts.\n📋 What Is It Like to Be an Emergency Manager? Meet professionals
  working in disaster and emergency management and explore possible career 
 pathways in public safety\, emergency planning\, risk reduction\, and comm
 unity resilience.\n🏢 Community Partner Showcase Connect with organizati
 ons working on disaster preparedness\, emergency response\, and humanitari
 an assistance\, including:\nCanadian Red Cross \nTeam Rubicon Canada \nEme
 rgency Management Ontario\nAdditional community and emergency management p
 artners\n🔍 Disaster Day Scavenger Hunt Explore the event while completi
 ng challenges and learning activities. All participants who complete the s
 cavenger hunt will be entered into a draw for a $100 prize.\nRegistration 
 is free\, but spaces are limited.\nregister today ( https://yorkliberalart
 s.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_40YrnhbM7STLS7A?Q_CHL=qr ) ! We hope you will 
 join us for an afternoon of learning\, exploration\, and discovery as we w
 ork together toward safer and more resilient communities.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261112
ORGANIZER;CN=ORU-Y-EMERGE:MAILTO:yemerge@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
