SUMMARY: Sonic Sancocho - Edición Simulacro Decembrino
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Drom Taberna with performances by Champetapunk and
  David Labrada Ensemble!\n\nWe're back at our beloved Drom Taberna for a 
 night celebrating autumn\, diverse sounds from across Latin America and o
 ur signature Sancocho - three things to keep your soul warm as the season
 s change.\n\nSonic Sancocho is thrilled to welcome special guest selector
  from Colombia\, Solano Patiño https://www.instagram.com/solanopatino/ \,
  who will deliver vibrant DJ sets to be broadcast live on his celebrated 
 radio show\, Champetapunk https://www.instagram.com/champetapunk/ \, and 
 live performances by Toronto-based\, acclaimed David Labrada Ensemble htt
 ps://www.instagram.com/david.labrada.1/ \, bringing the spirit of Havana 
 and flavours of the diasporas to the stage\, in sound.\n\nAs always\, Fou
 nders\, Juana Go-gó https://instagram.com/gogojuana and olasconola https:
 //instagram.com/olasconola will share a bold blend of music to welcome yo
 u to the party.\n\nComplimentary cup of Sancocho at midnight for ticket h
 olders - please note: first come\, first served.\n\nWhat is Sancocho? Lea
 rn more about the history here https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sancocho .\n
 \nAdvance Eventbrite ticket holders must check in to the venue by 10:30 p
 m.\n\nDate: Saturday\, November 21\, 2026\nDoors: 10:30 pm\nMusic: 11:00 
 pm - 4:00 am\nLocation: DROM Taberna - 458 Queen Street West\, Toronto\, 
 ON\, Canada\n\nAbout Sonic Sancocho:\nThe spice of life in sound\, shared
  with community. Much like ingredients in a universal dish - a big pot of
  soup - here\, platters of sound are spun and served with warm welcome. M
 usical ingredients from around the world\, from a local perspective\, for
  all to share and enjoy. Founded by selectresses olasconola http://instag
 ram.com/olasconola & http://instagram.com/gogojuana Juana Go-gó https://i
 nstagram.com/gogojuana in Toronto\, Canada\, Sonic Sancocho is a communit
 y gathering of music and food - two things that nourish heart and soul. T
 hey bring forth the B Sides and the beloved of Latin music\, with sounds 
 from around the world\, to your venue through all-vinyl DJ sets and dynam
 ic live performances. Sancocho is where all of the ingredients come toget
 her and are shared amongst one another - from the starches to the spices 
 and everything in between. We turn up the heat to bring it to a boil\, co
 ming together to enjoy a moment of connection through a serving of soup\,
  within layers of sound\, endless movement and fun.\n\nTune in to the rad
 io show https://ciut.fm/sonicsancocho/ \, hosted & produced by Juana Go-g
 ó https://instagram.com/gogojuana - Sundays at 2:00 pm ET on CIUT 89.5 FM
 !\n\nAbout Solano Patiño | Champetapunk:\n\nSolano Patiño is a selector\,
  record collector and researcher of Afro-Caribbean and world music. He is
  the founder and director of Radio Estruendo Tinansucá\, Bogotá’s free\, 
 experimental\, community-driven and portable radio\, and creator of Champ
 etapunk\, a party and research project on African diaspora culture and re
 bel sounds\, running since 2013 between Bogotá and Mexico City. His radio
  work has taken him across Asia\, Africa\, North Africa and the Caribbean
 \, where he has relentlessly dug through markets and record shops in sear
 ch of vinyl. This set is built mainly from those finds on 7″: Afro-Caribb
 ean and world music.\n\nAbout David Labrada:\nDavid Labrada More is a Tor
 onto-based performer\, composer\, music educator\, and music producer. He
  will be joining a roster of acclaimed pedagogues and guest artists in Au
 gust 2025 at The Royal Conservatory of Music’s inaugural Summer Piano Per
 formance Intensive for high school students\, where he will be teaching i
 mprovisation.\n\nDavid is an award-winning musician and composer\, winnin
 g First Place in the National Youth Jazz Competition in Havana\, Cuba thr
 ee years consecutively (2006-2008). As an educator with experience in bot
 h classroom and private instruction\, David teaches jazz piano\, voice\, 
 percussion\, music theory\, songwriting\, and music production. He has de
 veloped curriculum for private school music programs\, including ensemble
  direction for band and choir. He also has experience teaching music from
  Junior Kindergarten to Grade 8 as outlined by The Ontario Curriculum.\n\
 nFounder of DLM.Music Production\, David works with local and internation
 al artists including Ernesto del Alma (Canada)\, Irene Miguel (UK)\, Adon
 is Puentes (BC)\, Cassava Latin Band (Canada)\, Joel Sierra (Mexico)\, Ma
 rio y su timbeco (US)\, and Edglish (Azerbaijani).\n\nDavid has a Bachelo
 r of Music in Composition from Higher Institute of Art (Havana\, Cuba) an
 d a Bachelor of Arts in Music from the University of Toronto.
CATEGORIES:DJ/Club/Rave,DROM-Taberna,Concert
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/6755f3e6a02aaf
 1c2599e757/6af5279833339b9bfdb33ff5/scaled_1024.jpg
X-TKF-CUSTOM-PREVIEW:Join us at Drom Taberna with performances by Champet
