X-SOURCE-URLS:{"York University": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/pursue-peace-contemporary-chamber-music-by-canadian-jewish-composers-an-album-release-concert/", "Toronto Events (Tockify)": "https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/25040/1795377600000"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/pursue-peace-contemporary-chamber-music-by-canadian-jewish-composers-an-album-release-concert/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Pursue Peace: Contemporary Chamber Music by Canadian Jewish Compos
 ers\, An Album Release Concert
DTSTART:20261122T200000Z
DTEND:20261122T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20261109T182200Z
UID:MEC-2cb003b410ba24d03b9fc7fee7e2ad8a@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261122T200000Z
SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/1
 1/Pursue-Peace-landscape.png
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp\; Design
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261109
DESCRIPTION:Free admission. Register on our Eventbrite:\nhttps://www.event
 brite.ca/e/pursue-peace-contemporary-chamber-music-by-canadian-jewish-comp
 osers-tickets-2001068522819 ( https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/pursue-peace-con
 temporary-chamber-music-by-canadian-jewish-composers-tickets-2001068522819
  )\nAlbum Release Celebration Concert\nYork University’s Koschitzky Cent
 re for Jewish Studies and the Department of Music in the School of the Art
 s\, Media\, Performance and Design invite you to the opening of the fifth 
 season of Sound and Sense: Jewish Music at York\, with a special release c
 oncert celebrating Pursue Peace\, the initiative’s debut album. The prog
 ram brings together the work of three distinguished Canadian composers and
  leading performers in an evening of music shaped by memory\, identity\, h
 istory\, and the many ways music gives voice to human experience.\nRelease
 d by New Focus Recordings\, the New York-based independent label devoted t
 o contemporary and creative music\, Pursue Peace features composers Noam L
 emish (ON)\, Sid Robinovitch (MB)\, and James Rolfe (ON)\, whose music spa
 ns intimate works for violin and piano\, string quartet and clarinet\, and
  a larger work for choir\, soprano and ensemble.\nMore than three years in
  the making\, the album is the culmination of an ongoing artistic collabor
 ation at York\, bringing the work of Sound and Sense: Jewish Music at York
  to a wider audience. We invite you to join the ongoing conversation throu
 gh music and celebrate this milestone with us.\nFeaturing:\nAmy Hillis\, v
 iolin\, Katherine Dowling\, piano\, Sara Schabas\, soprano\, David Fallis\
 , conductor\, Maya Lahyani\, mezzo-soprano\, Noam Lemish\, piano\, Anthony
  Thompson\, clarinet\, Ilana Waniuk\, violin\, Carol Gimbel\, viola\, Mark
  Chambers\, cello\, Clark Schaufele\, chamber organ\, Nathan Petitpas\, pe
 rcussion\, Jane Fingler\, soprano\, Vania Chan\, soprano\, Veronika Mugger
 idge\, alto\, Rebecca Claborn\, alto\, Laura Chambers\, flute\, Cheryl Duv
 al\, piano.\nProgram:\nAdieu Babylon by Sid Robinovitch\nDi Mezinkeh by Si
 d Robinovitch\nPursue Peace by Noam Lemish\nSelections from Blood and Wate
 r by James Rolfe\nO Greenest Branch by James Rolfe\n“Sound and Sense: Je
 wish Music @ York” is a performance and lecture series dedicated to show
 casing the multicultural diversity of Jewish musical expression as well as
  the ongoing intersections between Jewish and non-Jewish musical practices
  and communities. The initiative is driven by an inclusive philosophy that
  believes in the power of music to serve as a bridge-builder and a vehicle
  for cultural exchange and dialogue.\nParking is available at the Student 
 Services Parking Garage (15 James Gillies St\, North York\, ON).\nThe Acco
 lade East Building is located immediately outside the York University subw
 ay station (TTC line 1) in front of the left hand exit.\nThe series has be
 en made possible via the generous support of the Azrieli Foundation.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109
LOCATION:Accolade East Building\, Tribute Communities Recital Hall @ 83 Yo
 rk Boulevard\, Toronto
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/pursue-peace-contemporary-chamber-music
 -by-canadian-jewish-composers-an-album-release-concert/
X-SOURCE:York University, Toronto Events (Tockify)
END:VEVENT
