SUMMARY:Geometric Art and Watercolours
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T150000
UID:6ac6de6d96ec3a003ad9124e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Geometric patterns are among the most recognizable visual expr
 essions of Islamic art and architecture. In the past\, craftsmen had an ex
 tensive practical knowledge of geometry. Nowadays\, we tend to rely heavil
 y on tools such as protractors\, compasses\, and rulers. In this workshop\
 , participants will be guided by artist Farooq Zia through step-by-step in
 structions using drawing tools and watercolour paint to create their own g
 eometric pattern and complex design art pieces.\nInformation Collection No
 tice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto P
 ublic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, an
 d 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrat
 ion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles you
 r information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\
 , 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Burrows Hall
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac6de6d96ec3a003ad9124e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
