DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T160000
UID:6a9c7ba8a3fb9722897a9587@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In late 16th-century England\, Agnes (Jessie Buckley)\, a heal
 er sensitive to the world around her\, builds a home with William (Paul Me
 scal)\, a local tutor and aspiring playwright. As their lives fracture\, t
 hey are tested by distance\, silence\, and grief. Based on the book\,\nHam
 net\nwritten by Maggie O’Farrell.\nPG\, 126 minutes\n**Subtitles for the
  deaf and hard of hearing when available (SDH).
LOCATION:Riverdale\, RD Program Room 1
