BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Torontojs": "https://www.meetup.com/torontojs/events/317276003/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_torontojs
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Toronto JavaScript
UID:event_317276003@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261114T061847Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T210000
SUMMARY:TechTalk (In-Person) - November 2026
DESCRIPTION:Toronto JavaScript\nHere’s the November edition of our Tech 
 Talk event at Super.com on November 24\, 2026.\n\nJoin us for some drinks\
 , snacks\, and Tech Talks.\n\nMake sure to mark your calendars\, come out\
 , and join us for this event!\n\n**🕑 Agenda & Schedule ✨**\n\n* 18:00
  - Doors open\n\n* 18:20 - Intro and announcements\n\n* 18:30 - **Attentio
 n Attention Everywhere** by **[Dev Shah](https://x.com/busycaesar)**\n*Abs
 tract:* In modern AI transformers\, "attention is all you need"—but what
  does it actually compute? Demystify the mechanism step by step using real
  numbers. Learn why tokens split into queries\, keys\, and values\, and ve
 rify the math against real GPT-2 weights\, including why heads focus on to
 ken #1. A technical walkthrough.\n\n* 19:00 - **Create an AI agent with Ve
 rcel AI SDK** by **[Emily Xiong](https://www.linkedin.com/in/xiongemi/)**\
 n*Abstract*: In this session\, I’ll share how I "vibe coded" a custom AI
  Code Reviewer using Next.js and the Vercel AI SDK. We will break down the
  core capabilities of the Vercel AI SDK\, comparing its unified approach t
 o the manual overhead of using direct LLM APIs like OpenAI or Gemini.\n\n*
  19:30 - **Beyond Motion Generation** by **Karin Fam**\n*Abstract*: AI can
  now generate an animation in seconds\, but generation is the easy part. T
 he real challenge starts when motion needs to ship consistently across doz
 ens of screens\, platforms\, and teams.\nIn this talk\, Karin looks at wha
 t comes after the prompt: how to think about animation as a system rather 
 than a one-off asset\, why scale and governance matter as much as creativi
 ty\, and how teams can build motion workflows that stay consistent\, perfo
 rmant\, and on-brand as they grow.\n\n* 20:00 - Networking\n\n* 21:00 - Do
 ors Close\n\n(**Note**: *All times in the schedule are an approximation.*)
 \n\nPlease RSVP to confirm your attendance. If you have your friends or te
 ammates joining please ask them to RSVP as well.\n\nThis event is open to 
 all skill levels.\n\nMany thanks to [Super.com](Super.com) for hosting us!
 \n\nWe're looking for sponsors for events like these. If you or your compa
 ny would like to support TorontoJS and get a message out to our community\
 , please get in touch with organizers@torontojs.com\n\nThe Code of Conduct
  is enforced at all TorontoJS events and spaces - online or in-person.\n\n
 TorontoJS is a volunteer-led not-for-profit organization.\n\n**Please help
  us** with tidying up. Otherwise\, the venue staff and volunteers will hav
 e to pick up after you.\n\\-\\-\\-\n\n# **The Venue 🏠**\n\nThe venue is
  next door to Shoppers Drug Mart\, a nondescript door that you'll have to 
 look for a little carefully.\n\\-\\-\\-\n*TorontoJS is committed to creati
 ng a safe and inclusive environment for all. Our Code of Conduct applies b
 oth online and in person at all our events and spaces.*\n\nSee you there! 
 🎉
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/torontojs/events/317276003/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261103T215838Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261103T215838Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
