ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/1
 1/MoreThanHumanEventImage@2x.png
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Environmental &amp\; Urban Change
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261109
DESCRIPTION:This talk will explore the critical connection between Indigen
 ous place-based knowledge and the relationships with the more-than-human w
 orld embedded in the Shuar landscape of the Ecuadorian Amazon. In this tal
 k\, Shuar leaders from the Ecuadorian Amazon will be at York University to
  share the importance of their science and the significance of the Shuar P
 eoples’ ability to interact with sacred Shuar sites\, songs and ceremoni
 es with the more-than-human world as a way to co-produce knowledge and und
 erstand more-than-human wisdom\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109
LOCATION:Health\, Nursing and Environmental Studies Building\, York Univer
 sity @ HNES Building
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
