X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Civic Tech Toronto": "https://guild.host/events/civic-meetup-570-invaders-qv0mzd"}
X-SOURCE-ID:guildhost_civic_tech
SUMMARY:Civic Meetup #570: "Invaders\,” “Polluters\,” and “Predato
 rs”: Anti-South Asian Racism in Canadian Far-Right Digital Networks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T210000
UID:64837b4118d4a4d4014a7befee43bdc2@guild.host
DESCRIPTION:Topic: "Invaders\,” “Polluters\,” and “Predators”: A
 nti-South Asian Racism in Canadian Far-Right Digital Networks\n\nHow do Ca
 nadian far-right groups portray South Asians on social media? Drawing on d
 ata collected from Canadian far-right networks on X (formerly Twitter)\, t
 he analysis focuses on depictions of South Asians as “invaders\,” “p
 olluters\,” and “predators\,” and explores how emotions like fear an
 d disgust are used​​ to frame South Asians as outsiders and perceived 
 threats to Canada.\n\n‎\n\nSpeaker: Dr. Zeinab Farokhi (in-person)\n\nDr
 . Zeinab Farokhi is an Assistant Professor of Women\, Gender\, and Sexuali
 ty Studies at the University of Toronto Mississauga. Her upcoming book\, D
 igital Islamophobia\,  explores the gendered and affective dimensions of a
 nti-Muslim sentiments across Canada\, the United States\, and India.\n\n
 ‎\n\nAgenda:\n\n7:00-7:20 Welcome and Introductions\n\n7:20-7:50 Present
 ation and Q\\&A/discussion\n\n7:50-9:00 Breakout groups\n\n‎\n\nCode of 
 Conduct: https://civictech.ca/about-us\n\n‎\n\nCheck in with us on the C
 ivic Tech Toronto Slack: https://link.civictech.ca/chat\n\n‎\n\nAbout Us
 :\n\nOur weekly civic meetups bring together Torontonians (designers\, cod
 ers\, urban planners\, government staff\, mappers\, policy-makers\, studen
 ts\, communications strategists\, community organizers\, and more) who sha
 re an interest in making Toronto more responsive\, prosperous\, sustainabl
 e\, and equitable through design\, tech\, and data.\n\nCome and be part of
  it!\n\nFor more info: https://civictech.ca\n\n\\--\n\nSuggest a Speaker:&
 #x20\;\n\nInterested in speaking at a future event\, or know someone who'd
  be a great speaker? We'd love to hear from you: https://link.civictech.ca
 /speaker-suggestions\n\nSuggest a Venue:&#x20\;\n\nHave a space that could
  host up to 80 civic-minded folks for an evening? Consider recommending yo
 ur venue: https://link.civictech.ca/venue-suggestions\n
LOCATION:Online: https://link.civictech.ca/zoom
URL:https://guild.host/events/civic-meetup-570-invaders-qv0mzd
X-SOURCE:Civic Tech Toronto
END:VEVENT
