BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/canoe-with-us-indigenous-education-research/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Canoe with Us? Indigenous Education & Research
DTSTART:20261124T203000Z
DTEND:20261124T221500Z
DTSTAMP:20261109T181700Z
UID:MEC-78f25aa54f838ebef52df7eb2f4dabd8@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261124T203000Z
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Education
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261109
DESCRIPTION:This panel discussion brings together Indigenous scholars to s
 hare insights\, experiences\, and future directions in education and resea
 rch. It serves as an invitation to all faculty and graduate students to bu
 ild relationships\, share common goals\, and explore future collaborations
 .\n Key Discussion Themes:\n\nFaculty Reflections: Personal insights into
  their journeys as Indigenous Faculty members.\nResearch Horizons: Current
  achievements and future research trajectories\nGraduate Support: Pathways
  for the mentorship and support of graduate students\nCollaborative Allian
 ces: Roles\, partnerships\, and meaningful collaborations with non-Indigen
 ous counterparts\n\n Facilitator:\n\nAngel Alook: Director of the Centre 
 for Indigenous Knowledges and Languages (CIKL)\, and Associate Professor i
 n the School of Gender\, Sexuality and Women’s Studies\n\nPanelists:\n\n
 John Hupfield: Wuleelham Director\, overseeing the Waaban Indigenous Teach
 er Education program\, examines powwow as a place to enact pedagogy\, prax
 is\, and knowledges in grounding community through culture and land\nRebec
 ca Beaulne-Stuebing: Assistant Professor whose research focuses on Indigen
 ous education and community-grounded learning\, including a community medi
 cines sovereignty project\nJesse Staats: Assistant Professor\, explores In
 digenous experiences and approaches to transforming governance relationshi
 ps between universities and Indigenous Peoples\n\nRSVP HERE\nPlease RSVP y
 our attendance to by November 19\, 2026.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109
LOCATION:280N York Lanes
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/canoe-with-us-indigenous-education-rese
 arch/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
