BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/canadian-writers-in-person-reading-series-we-the-kindling/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Canadian Writers in Person Reading Series: We\, The Kindling
DTSTART:20261125T000000Z
DTEND:20261125T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20261111T155600Z
UID:MEC-dee7539590036bbddca5ab8fc0b8357e@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261125T000000Z
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:LA&amp\;PS Department of Humanities
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261111
DESCRIPTION:Students get up close and personal with an eclectic group of a
 uthors while earning course credit through LA&PS’ Canadian Writers in Pe
 rson (AP/CLTR 1953 6.0A) course. They explore the contemporary work of ren
 owned authors\, while having the unique opportunity to engage with them in
  a dialogue about their work.\nReadings are free and open to members of th
 e public and to members of the York community not enrolled in the course.\
 nOur lineups consist of a unique selection of emerging and established Can
 adian writers\, whose writing explores a broad range of topics\, and a var
 iety of geographical and cultural landscapes. Featuring seasoned and emerg
 ing poets and fiction writers\, the series highlights Canada’s ever-grow
 ing literary talent.\nNovember 24th – Join us for a live reading of We\,
  the Kindling with Otoniya J. Okot Bitek tells the story of three women wh
 o survived abduction by the Lord’s Resistance Army in northern Uganda as
  children. Now adults\, they struggle with the lasting emotional and psych
 ological effects of their traumatic pasts while trying to build new lives 
 and families. Through vivid storytelling\, folk tales and multiple women
 ’s voices\, the novel explores war\, survival\, memory\, trauma and the 
 strength of human connection. Ultimately\, it is a moving and powerful sto
 ry about resilience\, love and the lasting impact of violence.https://www.
 yorku.ca/laps/huma/canadian-writers/ ( https://www.yorku.ca/laps/huma/cana
 dian-writers/ )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261111
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/canadian-writers-in-person-reading-seri
 es-we-the-kindling/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
