SUMMARY:Responding to Students in Distress for Teaching Assistants
DTSTART:20261126T150000Z
DTEND:20261126T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20261030T040100Z
UID:MEC-56909640f93a509bda9494a0178e091e@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261126T150000Z
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261029
DESCRIPTION:This workshop is carefully tailored to graduate students who a
 re teaching assistants or who will be starting a teaching assistantship at
  York University. This workshop will help teaching assistants identify spe
 cific signs that a student may be in distress\, what the referral options 
 are and how to communicate this information to distressed students in an a
 ppropriate way. Additional items that will be covered include how teaching
  assistants can support themselves while supporting their students. This w
 orkshop will take place virtually on Thursday November 26\, 2026 from 10:0
 0 am – 11:00 am. The zoom link will be provided after registration is co
 mpleted. If you are interested\, please register: Responding to Students i
 n Distress for Teaching Assistants (Fall 2026) – Fill out form\nIf you h
 ave any questions\, please email gradwell@yorku.ca.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261029
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
ORGANIZER;CN="Faculty of Graduate Studies":MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/responding-to-students-in-distress-for-
 teaching-assistants-2/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
