DESCRIPTION:The next chapter of AI in Canada. Everyone's conversation.\nDi
 scover Canada’s growing AI ecosystem at this full-day event\, exploring 
 homegrown innovation and what it means for our communities and the public 
 good.\nFrom policymakers and entrepreneurs to academics\, students and cur
 ious citizens\, this summit convenes voices from across Toronto to examine
  what it takes to shape a future rooted in responsible innovation and open
  access to knowledge.\nThe day will include:\nAn all-day forum with panels
  and discussions featuring leading voices from across Canada’s AI ecosys
 tem.\nA showcase for local innovators and organizations to exhibit their A
 I solutions\, innovations\, or programs.\nRegistration for the workshop is
  full\, but you can join the\nwaitlist\n.\nDiscover Canadian AI. Bring you
 r questions and perspectives. Join the conversation about what comes next.
  Visit\ntpl.ca/aisummit\nfor more information about the Summit.\nCan't att
 end in person? The conversations will be livestreamed.\nRegister to receiv
 e the viewing link\n.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice\n: The personal 
 information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under 
 the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informa
 tion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and e
 valuation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be
  directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-3975981\, 789 
 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\n***\nAccessibility at this event:\nAI 
 Summit Conversations will be presented with ASL interpreters and live capt
 ioning. For other supports\, refer to the information below.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Bram & Bluma Appel Salon and Beeton H
 all
