BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup A Book Club Downtown Abcd": "https://www.meetup.com/a-book-club-downtown-abcd/events/317308816/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_a_book_club_downtown_abcd
X-SOURCE:Meetup: A Book Club Downtown
UID:event_317308816@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261114T061834Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261128T213000
SUMMARY:ABCD Watches "The Gymnasts of Fisherman Colony" directed by Habiba
  Nosheen
DESCRIPTION:A Book Club\, Downtown (ABCD)\nYou're invited to a screening a
 t Hot Docs of ABCD Book Club member Habiba Nosheen's documentary ***[The G
 ymnasts of Fisherman Colony](https://www.thegymnastsoffishermancolony.com/
 )***. Register for the event and I'll send you a ***code for 20% off ticke
 ts***. We'll meet up beforehand\, and anyone interested can join us for dr
 inks afterwards.\n\n*"The Gymnasts of Fisherman Colony is an intimate comi
 ng-of-age documentary by three-time Emmy Award–winning filmmaker Habiba 
 Nosheen that follows three teenage girls in Pakistan\, offering a rare and
  tender portrait of girlhood\, joy\, and play told through the eyes of you
 ng Pakistani girls navigating the margins of society.*\n*At its core\, The
  Gymnasts of Fisherman Colony is a story of hope and quiet defiance. Throu
 gh the intimate journeys of three teenagers we witness as their passion fo
 r gymnastics begins to clash with deeply rooted expectations around what g
 irls can and cannot do. The film follows their journey as they find themse
 lves straddling two polar opposite worlds as they push to make space for t
 hemselves through gymnastics. The result is a lyrical and deeply human por
 trait of three young girls from a corner of the world we rarely see on scr
 een. These are girls who dare to dream."* (from the [Hot Docs](https://box
 office.hotdocs.ca/websales/pages/info.aspx?evtinfo=658891~cf285ddd-dacb-4f
 18-89b8-1252c6dcffa6&epguid=a2104450-7e47-4369-a17d-c247570c3939&mdy=11/28
 /2026&) website)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/a-book-club-downtown-abcd/events/3173
 08816/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261106T024006Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261106T024006Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
