SUMMARY:What is Artificial Intelligence?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T153000
UID:6aad8fb8129d8e0031f35a26@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI technologies have become increasingly prevalent in many asp
 ects of modern life\, including healthcare\, finance\, transportation\, an
 d entertainment.  Some examples of AL applications include virtual assist
 ants like Siri and Alexa\, self-driving cars\, fraud detection systems\, a
 nd personalized recommendations in online shopping.  Come join this begin
 ner in-person class to learn what AI is\, how it learns and predicts outco
 mes\, considerations when using GenAI applications\, and how the Internet 
 of Things (IOT) applies to AI.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe person
 al information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library und
 er the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The info
 rmation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery an
 d evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can
  be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 
 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aad8fb8129d8e0031f35a26
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
