SUMMARY:Pressed Flowers Necklace Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261130T160000
UID:6af4acbb4896360041d0d1a9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Capture summer’s beauty forever in this hands-on Flower Pres
 sed Necklace Workshop\, hosted by Gabriela Delworth. Whether you're a jewe
 lry enthusiast or a nature lover\, this session offers a creative space to
  design a wearable piece of art that lasts forever.\nWhat You Will Discove
 r:\nThe Art of Pressing: Learn the essential techniques for preserving blo
 oms\, including the best time of day to harvest and which flower varieties
  hold their color and shape best.\nStorage Secrets: Master the professiona
 l methods for storing pressed flowers to prevent fading and moisture damag
 e.\nJewelry Design: Arrange your choice of delicate petals and greenery in
 to a custom pendant. You will leave with a one-of-a-kind necklace that res
 pects your personal style.\nWorkshop Details:\nTools are provided by the i
 nstructor and returned at the end of the workshop.\nSkill Level: Perfect f
 or beginners\; no prior experience in jewelry making or gardening is requi
 red.\nSpace is limited.  Registration is required.\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice: The personal information on this form is collected by the Toront
 o Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\,
  and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regist
 ration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles 
 your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\
 , 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af4acbb4896360041d0d1a9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
