SUMMARY:Fourth Annual National DIVERT Meeting
DTSTART:20261201T140000Z
DTEND:20261201T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20261019T200900Z
UID:MEC-e06e5fef737c2b369a295d2b22fa1b1f@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261201T140000Z
SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/1
 0/2026-Eventbrite-Background-OPEN-3-1.png
CATEGORIES:Artificial Intelligence,Equity, Diversity &amp\; Inclusion,Facu
 lty of Health,Research &amp\; Innovation,Well-being,YFile newsletter
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261019
DESCRIPTION:Join DIVERT Mental Health on December 1\, 2026\, for the publi
 c day of its Fourth Annual National Meeting at York University in Toronto\
 , with in-person and virtual attendance options.\nDIVERT Mental Health is 
 a national CIHR-funded research training platform led by York University
 ’s Dr. Rebecca Pillai Riddell\, focused on inclusive mental health resea
 rch and digital innovation.\nThe program brings together researchers\, cli
 nicians\, trainees and community partners to explore youth mental health\,
  including eating disorders\, screen use\, digital mental health and 2SLGB
 TQ+ youth\, and equity in mental health research and policy.\nDate: Tuesda
 y\, December 1\, 2026\nTime: 9:00 a.m.–5:00 p.m. Eastern Time\nRegistrat
 ion: $25 for in-person attendance or $15 for virtual attendance.\nRegistra
 tion is now open. Please visit the links below to register and explore the
  agenda and speaker information.\nRegister through Eventbrite ( https://ww
 w.eventbrite.ca/e/fourth-annual-national-divert-meeting-tickets-2002573498
 241?aff=oddtdtcreator )\nView the agenda and speakers ( https://divertment
 alhealth.ca/fourth-annual-national-divert-meeting-agenda-final/ )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261019
LOCATION:Second Student Centre
ORGANIZER;CN="DIVERT Mental Health":MAILTO:divert@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/fourth-annual-national-divert-meeting/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
