SUMMARY: Silkworm + Fines: Wavelength
DESCRIPTION:Presented with Sonic Boom\n\nIn partnership with TO Live\n\n\
 nSilkworm\n\n(Chicago // American indie-rock icons & Steve Albini collabo
 rators)\n\n\nFines (Darcy Hancock of Ladyhawk)\n\n(Vancouver // Canadian 
 indie hero’s solo songwriting project)\n\n\nDecember 3\, 2026\n\nWaveleng
 th @ St. Anne’s\n651 Dufferin St.\n\nDoors 7:30pm\n\nAll Ages\n\n\nSingle
  tix $32 plus taxes & fees at DICE.FM http://dice.fm\n\n25 and under PWYC
 ! (25 tickets online\, 25 tickets available at the door (pending capacity
  - must arrive by 8pm to claim)\nTicket link: http://bit.ly/SilkwormWL\n\
 n\nOn sale now!\n\n\nStoried and influential American indie-rock band Sil
 kworm comes back to Toronto for the first time in 26 years!\n\n\nFormed i
 n 1987\, Silkworm is revered by those in the know. Relocating from Missou
 la\, Montana to Seattle and eventually Chicago\, the band has released ni
 ne acclaimed albums on iconic labels including Matador and Touch and Go R
 ecords. They disbanded in 2005 following drummer Michael Dahlquist tragic
  passing\, and reunited in 2024 to honour their late friend and collabora
 tor Steve Albini\, joined by drummer Jeff Panall (Songs: Ohia\, Mint Mile
 ). Playing together as a quartet for the first time in 30 years proved bo
 th emotional and exhilarating\, inspiring a long-awaited return to the st
 age.\n\nThe band's enduring legacy is celebrated in the documentary Could
 n't You Wait: The Story of Silkworm and the forthcoming book Lay It Down 
 in Full View.\n\nFor their historic return to Toronto\, Silkworm will be 
 joined by Fines\, the songwriting project of Darcy Hancock. Many listener
 s will remember Hancock as a member of Vancouver’s indie-rock favourites\
 , Ladyhawk\, whose records and non-stop touring helped establish them as 
 one of Canada's most beloved guitar bands of the 2000s.\n\nPoster by Juli
 a Araïche\n\n
CATEGORIES:Wavelength,Concert,St.-Anne's-Parish-Hall
