SUMMARY: GenTO: Toronto AI Film Festival
DESCRIPTION:GenTO: Toronto AI Film Festival is a celebration of the emerg
 ing world of AI-enhanced filmmaking\, bringing together filmmakers\, arti
 sts\, creative technologists and film enthusiasts to explore the evolving
  possibilities of cinematic storytelling.\n\nTaking place on December 5\,
  2026\, at Innis Town Hall\, University of Toronto\, the festival showcas
 es a curated selection of AI-assisted short films\, advertisements and mu
 sic videos from creators around the world\, alongside filmmaker Q&As\, in
 dustry panels\, behind-the-scenes discussions\, networking opportunities 
 and an awards ceremony recognizing creative excellence.\n\nAs AI filmmaki
 ng gains momentum in Toronto and across Canada\, GenTO provides a platfor
 m for the growing community of creators to showcase their work\, exchange
  ideas and connect with industry professionals. By bringing international
  perspectives to Toronto's vibrant film culture\, the festival aims to fo
 ster dialogue\, experimentation and collaboration at the intersection of 
 filmmaking and emerging technology.\n\nThe festival offers filmmakers and
  creative professionals opportunities to discover emerging storytelling t
 echniques\, engage with industry peers and build meaningful connections\,
  while inviting film enthusiasts to experience new forms of cinematic exp
 ression and explore the future of filmmaking.\n\nMore Info: gento.ca/fest
 ival https://gento.ca/festival
CATEGORIES:Film,Innis-Town-Hall
