DESCRIPTION:In this session:\nlearn what credit is and how it      works\n
 understand the difference      between good debt and bad debt\nthe cost of
  debt\, particularly      bad debt and only making minimum payments\nhow p
 ayday loan companies      operate and the cost of borrowing from them\nund
 erstand how debt can pile up      and how this can have negative consequen
 ces on future financial plans\nlearn how to take control of      debt\, in
 cluding assessing the amount of debt\, debt repayment options\,      deali
 ng with creditors\, and collection agencies and rules\nPresented by Charte
 red Professional Accountants Canada\nInformation Collection Notice: The pe
 rsonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library
  under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The 
 information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliver
 y and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information
  can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-598
 1\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201\, 2nd Floor.
