X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aeb8f7c035faf0033e16452"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Mythology and folklore reading group: Gifts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T201500
UID:6aeb8f7c035faf0033e16452@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Our November session will include stories on the theme Gifts
  from around the world.\nToronto Reference Library invites you to join th
 e Mythology and Folktale reading group. The group will meet once a month t
 o read aloud and discuss famous and lesser known myths. No pre-reading req
 uired\, beginners welcome.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal i
 nformation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under t
 he Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informat
 ion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and ev
 aluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be 
 directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 
 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Founder's room\, 1st floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aeb8f7c035faf0033e16452
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 School Age": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac5874da85a2c00337db3b3"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_school_age
SUMMARY:Classical & Latin American Guitar Performance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261208T193000
UID:6ac5874da85a2c00337db3b3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Karla García is a Chilean-Canadian guitarist\, music creator\
 , and educator based in Toronto. Originally from Chiloé\, Chile\, she ha
 s performed as a soloist and collaborator with orchestras and ensembles in
  Canada and Latin America. Her musical work brings together classical guit
 ar\, Latin American music\, popular music\, and original songs. Karla stud
 ied guitar at the University of Chile and has performed with orchestras in
 cluding the Ontario Pops Orchestra and the Scarborough Philharmonic Orches
 tra. As an educator\, she is passionate about creating welcoming and engag
 ing learning experiences that help students develop confidence and a lasti
 ng connection with music.\nNo registration required\, all are welcome\n!
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac5874da85a2c00337db3b3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
