SUMMARY:[In]Security: Military Portraiture of Gertrude Kearns
DTSTART:20261210T173000Z
DTEND:20270102T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20261111T210900Z
UID:MEC-29093d10b0c57f776c78f839d0203739@events.yorku.ca__20261210
SEQUENCE:4
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 11/ARTH4110-Poster_Page_2-1-scaled.jpg
CATEGORIES:Advancement/Alumni,Bethune College,Calumet College,Colleges,Div
 isions and Special Areas,Equity, Diversity &amp\; Inclusion,Equity, People
  &amp\; Culture,Faculties,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Graduate Program in 
 Art History,Graduate Program in Visual Art,Recruitment,Regional Alumni Eve
 nts,Stong College,Students,YFile newsletter
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261111
DESCRIPTION:[In] Security\, evokes the tensions between protection and vul
 nerability\, certainty and instability. Made between 2002 and 2026\, these
  works are portraits of real people: Canadian Armed Forces senior officers
  at critical moments in Canada’s military history. They are also records
  of the systems around them. Uniforms\, maps\, borders\, slogans\, insigni
 a and military jargon move the image beyond likeness\, locating the indivi
 dual within larger structures of geography\, conflict and institutional po
 wer.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261111
LOCATION:Joan Goldfarb Study Centre\, 275 Joan &amp\; Martin Goldfarb Cent
 re for Fine Arts @ 86 Fine Arts Road\, Toronto
ORGANIZER;CN="Department of Visual Art and Art History":MAILTO:
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/insecurity-military-portraiture-of-gert
 rude-kearns-2/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Toronto Enterprise Devops User Group": "https://www.meetup.com/toronto-enterprise-devops-user-group/events/316393777/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_toronto_enterprise_devops_user_group
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Toronto Enterprise DevOps
UID:event_316393777@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261114T061846Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T193000
SUMMARY:How to 10x Your DevOps with AI (Without Deleting Production)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Enterprise DevOps User Group\nAutopilot made flying sa
 fer\, not because the autopilot is perfect\, but because of the instrument
 s\, checklists\, and feedback around it. AI coding agents like Claude Code
 \, Codex\, and Cursor are no different. Too many teams are betting on bett
 er models and longer prompts\, when what agents actually need is the borin
 g stuff DevOps has preached for years: fast feedback\, deterministic check
 s\, and tight controls.\n\nAn AI coding tool reportedly deleted and recrea
 ted an AWS environment. Another wiped a production database during a code 
 freeze. Skipping the checks in "YOLO mode" is fast\, right up until it isn
 't. This talk is about the alternative: doubling down on DevOps in the age
  of AI\, so teams can move faster with agents inside locked-down enterpris
 e environments\, without betting production on a prompt. When developers w
 ith AI commit faster than ever\, the pipeline becomes the bottleneck. We'l
 l look at how to unblock them with fast CI/CD in GitHub Actions and on-dem
 and cloud environments. Then we'll get practical: how to 10x your delivery
  with modern AI tooling\, including Claude Code\, voice-driven development
 \, remote access\, and running agents in parallel.\n\nYou'll leave with:\n
 \\- Real takeaways for going fast and safe with AI agents\\\, from GitHub 
 Actions pipelines to cloud environments\n\\- How to 10x your DevOps workfl
 ow with Claude Code\\\, voice\\\, and remote access\n\n*Come at 5:30 pm ha
 ve some pizza and chat for a bit. The presentation starts at 6:00 pm.*
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-enterprise-devops-user-group/
 events/316393777/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260902T234717Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260902T234717Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
