DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261211T150000
UID:6adccca111bbf300684d246b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have fun learning a new instrument - the ukulele! Join music t
 eacher Meghan Gallant to learn the fundamentals of ukulele playing: the pa
 rts of a ukulele\, tuning\, strumming patterns\, and some basic chords. By
  the end of this class\, you'll have learned the skills you need to start 
 playing your first songs on the ukulele!\nBeginner friendly\, no previous 
 experience necessary. Ukuleles provided.\nSpaces are limited\, registratio
 n is required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information o
 n this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Li
 braries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will onl
 y be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Qu
 estions about how the library handles your information can be directed to 
 Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room (2nd Floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6adccca111bbf300684d246b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
