X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Seniors' Social: Calm & Canvas
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261211T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261211T153000
UID:6ada739febad2200454742b4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a fun and relaxing program just for SENIORS and OL
 DER ADULTS! Our Senior Club program includes simple exercises to support y
 our health\, engaging puzzles and brain games for mental stimulation\, dig
 ital learning classes to build new skills\, crafts\, and opportunities to 
 socialize\, share experiences\, and make new friends.\nEnjoy a fun and rel
 axing acrylic painting session designed for seniors and older adults. Expl
 ore your creativity\, experiment with colors\, and create simple\, enjoyab
 le artwork in a friendly and supportive environment. No painting experienc
 e is needed. Come socialize\, have fun\, and express yourself through art 
 at your own pace.\nThis program is intended for seniors and older adults. 
 Registration spots not claimed within 5 minutes of the program start time 
 may be given to drop-in participants.
LOCATION:Steeles
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ada739febad2200454742b4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a77508ac80d09476c935662"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Tea and Entertainment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261211T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261211T160000
UID:6a77508ac80d09476c935662@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy watching DVDs in the Library Auditorium.\nCoffee\, tea a
 nd cookies or snacks will be served after the film.  Ingredient lists wil
 l be available upon request.\nWill A Robot Steal My Job?\nArtificial intel
 ligence is changing the way people work and may replace many jobs\, includ
 ing those of professionals like lawyers\, accountants\, and artists. This 
 film discusses both the challenges of job loss and the possibility of adap
 ting to and benefiting from new technology. 52 minutes.2023
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a77508ac80d09476c935662
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
