SUMMARY:Search & Rescue Operations with Drone
DTSTART:20261212T143000Z
DTEND:20261212T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20261109T182400Z
UID:MEC-b5a568bf143bb0d356faadd0b7b592b3@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261212T143000Z
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp\; Career Centre,Colleges,Divisions and Special Areas
 ,Faculties,Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Progra
 ms),Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp\; Professional Studies,Future Students,Gl
 endon,Graduate Program in Disaster &amp\; Emergency Management,Graduate Pr
 ogram in Interdisciplinary Studies,LA&amp\;PS Alumni,LA&amp\;PS Colleges,L
 A&amp\;PS Students All,LA&amp\;PS Students-Graduate,LA&amp\;PS Students-In
 ternational,LA&amp\;PS Students-Undergrad,Lassonde School of Engineering,M
 arkham Campus,ORUs,Research &amp\; Innovation,Skill Development (CCC),Stud
 ents,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students,Workshops &amp\
 ; Webinars (CCC),YFile newsletter
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261109
DESCRIPTION:This intensive professional course\, offered by CIFAL York and
  ADERSIM\, is mainly designed for licensed drone pilots seeking to special
 ize in Search and Rescue (SAR) operations. Participants will move beyond b
 asic flight skills to master the strategic\, technical\, and analytical co
 mpetencies required for effective use of drone for various search and resc
 ue missions. With a practical focus on the powerful DJI Matrice 30T platfo
 rm\, this course integrates established SAR principles with cutting-edge d
 rone technology to prepare you for real-world scenarios.\nA certificate of
  completion will be issued to all participants from CIFAL York upon comple
 tion of the course.\n👥 Eligibility: Open to everyone (no prior SAR expe
 rience required).\n🎓 Student Perk: Special DISCOUNT for full-time stude
 nts\n⚠️ Seats are limited to ensure all participants receive dedicated
  flight practice time\n🔗 Registration and More Info ( https://www.yorku
 .ca/cifal/sar-d/ )\n⏳ Registration closes Thursday\, December 10.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109
LOCATION:Room N004 Schulich School of Business Building (Basement Floor)
ORGANIZER;CN="CIFAL York":MAILTO:cifalpresident@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/search-rescue-operations-with-drone/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
