SUMMARY: Songs of My Mother: A Celebration of African Women Concert
DESCRIPTION:Batuki Music Society presents Songs of My Mother: A Celebrati
 on of African Women at the Redwood Theatre on Saturday December 12th at 8
  pm. Doors open at 7 pm.\n\nThree electrifying vocalists and a dancer wit
 h roots on the African continent will honour the role of women and mother
 s in carrying on musical traditions.\n\nSongs of My Mother: A Celebration
  of African Women\, curated by Batuki Music Society will showcase diverse
  stories and musical styles from different regions of sub-Saharan Africa.
  Featured will be JUNO Award winners\, South African-born Lorraine Klaase
 n and Malian-born Djely Tapa\, also on the line-up is Melat Mengesha\, wi
 nner of the Balageru (Ethiopian Idol) and Guinea-born dancer Mabinty Syll
 a. These women share their unique talents in a showcase of musical divers
 ity and artistic excellence\, supported by an ensemble of accomplished mu
 sicians from Toronto and Montreal.\n\nThis presentation shines a light on
  female singers and their significance in African customs\, rituals and c
 eremonies. The first words or language that a child hears from their moth
 er are often shared in song. This introduction to sound and words through
  song is a very common element in the bonding process between a mother an
 d her newborn in most African cultures. Though singing is not solely done
  by women in most African societies\, it is true that the female voice is
  ever present and sometimes is not given a prominent role that it deserve
 s. Women are often discouraged from assuming leading roles\, especially a
 s bandleaders.\n\nMore than just an unforgettable evening of music and st
 orytelling\, Songs of My Mother aims to inspire mothers\, daughters\, gra
 ndmothers\, sisters\, and aunts to stand together and celebrate themselve
 s as major contributors to the arts and the community.\n\nSongs of My Mot
 her: Lorraine Klaasen\, Djely Tapa\, Melat Mengesha\, Mabinty Sylla\n\nDa
 te: Saturday\, December 12\, 2026 at 8 pm\n\nThe Redwood Theatre\, 1300 G
 errard St. East\, Toronto\n\nDoors: 7:00 pm Concert: 8:00 pm\n\nPrice: Ad
 vance $25 Door Tickets $30.\n\nhttps://SongsOfMother12DEC26.eventbrite.ca
  https://SongsOfMother12DEC26.eventbrite.ca\n\nhttp://batukimusic.com/sit
 e2 http://batukimusic.com/site2\n\n
CATEGORIES:Concert,Dance---Performance---Theatre,The-Redwood
