SUMMARY:Seniors E-Connect
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261215T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261215T173000
UID:6aa2e70aab7a8e0037c0cdc5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Seniors E-Connect matches older adults with a teen volunteer t
 o provide tech help\, under the guidance of library staff. Learn the basic
 s of using smartphone and laptop. Learn about topics such as\nsmartphone 
 accessibility features\, smartphone basics\, using search engine and googl
 e AI\, downloading PDF's and email attachment and many more\n. Seniors may
  bring their own device and ask our teens volunteers for tech help. Get 
 one on one support in a welcoming and friendly environment.\nIf you're a t
 een between the ages of 13-17 and would like to learn more about becoming 
 a Seniors E-Connect volunteer\, visit the\nSeniors E-Connect Volunteering 
 page\nor email\nBeaches Branch\nbestaff@tpl.ca\n.\nInformation Collection 
 Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto
  Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, 
 and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registr
 ation\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles y
 our information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\
 n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Beaches\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa2e70aab7a8e0037c0cdc5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
