SUMMARY:Island Soul:  A Caribbean Holiday Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T140000
UID:6af219edfb96d55bb889d6b8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Jamaican-Canadian guitarist\, educator\, and Afro-Jamaican ora
 l artist\nMaurice Gordon\ninvites you to a festive holiday presentation b
 ringing together live music\, storytelling\, conversation\, to explore the
  African roots and enduring influences woven throughout Jamaican history\,
  culture\, spirituality\, language\, and folklore.\nCelebrate the holiday 
 season with a vibrant musical and cultural journey into Jamaica’s rich A
 frican heritage and traditions at Mount Dennis!\nDrop-in\; no registration
  required\nMaurice Gordon\, B.A. (York U\, 1987) guitarist\, singer\, and 
 cultural researcher specializing in the ethnomusicology of Jamaican\, Blac
 k\, and Canadian traditions.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis\, Lower Level\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af219edfb96d55bb889d6b8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
