SUMMARY:North York Central Library Film Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T161500
UID:6af23eb0ad4027659156bb44@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for an afternoon screening of "Michael".\nMicha
 el\n(2026)\nRunning time: 127 minutes\nDirector: Antoine Fuqua\nStarring: 
 Jaafar Jackson\, Juliano Valdi\, Colman Domingo\, and Nia Long\nThe film t
 ells the story of early life of musician Michael Jackson\, from the discov
 ery of his talent as the lead of the Jackson Five to the artist. His creat
 ive ambition fueled a pursuit to become the biggest entertainer in the wor
 ld.\nThe North York Central Library Film Club meets monthly on Wednesdays.
  There is a short\, informal discussion after the screening\, time permitt
 ing.\nRegistration is not required. Please contact the Browsery Department
  at 416-395-5672 for more information.\nNext dates: Jan 20\, Feb 17
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af23eb0ad4027659156bb44
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
