X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:"Writing a Novel When You Don't Have Time to Write a Novel" with H
 eather Babcock
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T200000
UID:6af5d24e6d7b4d002c6713d9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:While writing her debut novel\nFilthy Sugar\n(Inanna Publicati
 ons\, published Spring 2020)\, Heather Babcock was working long and irregu
 lar shifts at her day job. With her understanding of how difficult it can 
 be to make the time to write when you are exhausted and/or have other comm
 itments\, Heather —whose next book\nThe Memory of Crows\nis forthcoming 
 from DarkWinter Press—shares tips and advice that she discovered along t
 he journey of writing her first novel.\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Wychwood\, Program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af5d24e6d7b4d002c6713d9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
