UID:event_316438898@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261114T061841Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261220T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261220T160000
SUMMARY:Mission of Gravity - Hal Clement
DESCRIPTION:The Sci Fi Book Club\nHi everybody\,\n\nBack for another team 
 investigating an alien planet. This time we have a true classic\, Hal Clem
 ent's seminal 1954 gritty sci fi novel\, *Missions of Gravity*. This one h
 as been on the list for a while and I'm so glad it was on theme enough to 
 get on the survey.\n\nBook of the Month\n*Mission of Gravity* \\- Hal Clem
 ent \\(1954\\)\n\nFrom a good review on Skiffy.ca\, "Originally serialized
  in 1953 in the magazine *[Astounding Science Fiction](https://en.wikipedi
 a.org/wiki/Analog_Science_Fiction_and_Fact)*\, the tale was published in b
 ook form the following year. Decades later\, it was awarded a [Retro Hugo]
 (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugo_Award#Retro_Hugos)\, for excellence in
  SF’s pioneering era.\n\n*Mission of Gravity* is an archetypal example o
 f what the kids call “hard science fiction”\, a subgenre in which the 
 characters within the SF story solve physical problems with physical –la
 rgely technological– means. The science tends to be solid\, even the spe
 culative science\, and the rules are intensely consistent within the bound
 aries of the story."\n\nTo join a Book Club meeting\, all you will need is
  YOURSELF. If you haven’t had a chance to finish the book\, we still wou
 ld love for you to join us in the discussion.\n\nNot able to join us in pe
 rson for events? [The Sci Fi Book Club is on Discord](https://discord.gg/B
 9NMnC2F). Join us and keep the conversation going.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/thescifibookclub/events/316438898/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260906T025016Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260906T025016Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad649ac29c3d6003330fc11"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Apple Devices for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261220T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261220T153000
UID:6ad649ac29c3d6003330fc11@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This class is for absolute beginners who are curious about buy
 ing an Apple iPhone or iPad\, or who have just acquired one and want to un
 derstand how it operates.\n\nIn this beginner’s class you will learn abo
 ut:\n-the different parts of an Apple iPhone or iPad and where they are lo
 cated\n-what you need to make your iPhone or iPad run\n-the Apple home scr
 een\n-settings\, storage and troubleshooting\n\nAt the end of the class yo
 u will have a basic understanding of how to run your Apple device and wher
 e to find what you are looking for on your Apple device.\n\nBring your own
  device:  if you have an Apple device\, feel free to bring it with you and
  follow along with the exercises.\n\nPrerequisites:  None\nFormat:  Lectur
 e with hands-on exercises\n[90 min]\n\nInformation Collection Notice: The 
 personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libra
 ry under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). Th
 e information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliv
 ery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informati
 on can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad649ac29c3d6003330fc11
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
