SUMMARY:Film Screening: The Booksellers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261222T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261222T201500
UID:6af7421204009d003388441a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A documentary exploration of the rare book trade featuring int
 erviews with an eclectic group of New York dealers and collectors.\nThey s
 hare their stories of finding their passion\, discuss the history of the 
 trade\, and the historical and social significance of book collections.\nT
 he film includes a discussion of what the future may look like as technolo
 gies change and a new generation discovers this centuries-old calling.\nA
  warm film for book lovers set to great jazz!
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, ground floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af7421204009d003388441a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
