BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Aga Khan Museum": "https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-holiday-metal-embossing/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:agakhan_museum
SUMMARY:Metal Embossing: Patterns for the Page
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T110000
UID:metal-embossing-patterns-for-the-page-2026-12-30t11-00-00-05-00@agakha
 nmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/11
 /Metal_Embossing_Bookmark_Shirin_Divanbeigi4-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000
 -scaled.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Through this hands-on workshop\, discover the art of metal emb
 ossing inspired by the patterns and craftsmanship found in the Aga Khan Mu
 seum’s Collections.\n\nWorking with copper\, participants will learn sim
 ple yet effective techniques to shape and decorate metal surfaces. Guided 
 by our Museum Educators\, you’ll design and create your own embossed boo
 kmark\, exploring how artists across the Islamic world have transformed me
 tal into objects of both beauty and function for centuries.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-holiday-metal-embossing/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Aga Khan Museum": "https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-holiday-clay-tile-workshop/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Aga Khan Museum": "https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-holiday-clay-tile-workshop/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:agakhan_museum
SUMMARY:Clay Tile Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T110000
UID:clay-tile-workshop-2026-12-30t11-00-00-05-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/11
 /Clay_Paid_Workshop_Shirin_Divanbeigi27-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scal
 ed.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Experiment with clay and craft your own unique tile in this ha
 nds-on workshop designed for both beginners and art enthusiasts.\n\nGuided
  by our Museum Educators\, participants will explore shaping\, designing\,
  and decorating techniques inspired by ceramic works in the Aga Khan Museu
 m’s Collections. Learn how patterns and motifs have been used for centur
 ies across the Islamic world\, and experiment with tools and textures to b
 ring your vision to life. You’ll leave with a one-of-a-kind creation tha
 t blends traditional inspiration with your own creativity.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-holiday-clay-tile-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
