UID:6af1f3133c35b95bcb2ab797@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A class on using Google's filters\, tools\, and Maps for absol
 ute beginners with little computer experience.\nIn this fourth session you
  will:\nUse Google search tools more effectively to find websites\, images
 \, and news sites\nExplore Google Maps to find addresses and get direction
 s for transit and road travel.\nUpon completion of this class students wil
 l be able to use more advanced search engine features and use Google Maps 
 at a basic level.\nPrerequisites: Computers for Beginners 1\, 2 & 3 or bas
 ic mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills\nFormat: Hands-on with demonstr
 ations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this f
 orm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries 
 Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be use
 d for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions 
 about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerli
 ne staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toron
 to ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Learning Center
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6af1f3133c35b95bcb2ab797
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
