BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/beyond-the-academy-2027/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Beyond the Academy 2027
DTSTART:20270111T150000Z
DTEND:20270111T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20261110T165800Z
UID:MEC-435c53251dc1f41d8d6b80f8592f6650@events.yorku.ca__20270111
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:LA&amp\;PS Colleges,LA&amp\;PS Students-Graduate
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261110
DESCRIPTION:Beyond the Academy is a five-week applied professional develop
 ment program designed to help LA&PS PhD students:\n• Understand the land
 scape of non-academic careers.\n• Reflect on personal values and strengt
 hs.\n• Translate academic experience into professional competencies.\n
 • Build professional networks and online presence.\n• Develop concrete
  strategies for career exploration and job searching.\nThe program will be
  cohort-based\, combining reflective exercises\, practical workshops\, and
  alumni engagement. It will culminate in an actionable career plan and pro
 fessional online profile for each participant.\nTo apply to the program\, 
 please complete the required registration form:\nBeyond the Academy Regist
 ration Form\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261110
ORGANIZER;CN="Marco Sestito":MAILTO:msestito@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/beyond-the-academy-2027/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aed1c019dbc2b002c93b347"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Walking\, Swimming\, Flying - Hands-On Nature
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270111T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270111T173000
UID:6aed1c019dbc2b002c93b347@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Explore the different ways organisms move (and moved) around o
 n Planet Earth. Some walk\, some swim\, and others fly. Can you tell which
  is which? Participants will be able to handle\, study and learn about str
 ange objects: fossils\, replicas and modern specimens. They will be guides
  all through the how\, when and why these organisms adapted to move as the
 y do. Interactive\, entertaining and educational\, join us for a journey i
 n living locomotion.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hub
 s are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the summer\, where h
 elpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered d
 aily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out 
 more.
LOCATION:Cedarbrae\, Youth Hub\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aed1c019dbc2b002c93b347
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
