BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/applied-qualitative-research/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Applied Qualitative Research: A Practical Guide for Graduate Stude
 nt Researchers
DTSTART:20270112T160000Z
DTEND:20270112T171500Z
DTSTAMP:20260818T205800Z
UID:MEC-650cee762ff8291600de84b1ba99f5a4@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20270112T160000Z
SEQUENCE:3
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/
 12/pexels-cottonbro-studio-9400300-2-scaled.jpg
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260818
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in gaining an understanding of how to desig
 n\, conduct\, and present applied qualitative research? If so\, these onli
 ne workshops are for you! While this series is particularly intended for g
 raduate students\, FGS additionally invites and warmly welcomes graduate f
 aculty including supervisors and committee members\, as well as research s
 taff\, and postdocs. Feel free to come to one\, two or all of them! Worksh
 ops will be delivered virtually and will be recorded. Registration is requ
 ired.\nFacilitated by Dr. Karen Campbell\, RN\, PhD ( https://www.linkedin
 .com/in/kcamp232/?originalSubdomain=ca )\, Assistant Professor\, School of
  Nursing\, York University. Dr. Campbell’s program of research focuses o
 n the intersections of women’s health with physical and social geography
 . She has taught graduate-level courses in qualitative research and design
 ed and conducted multiple applied qualitative research projects using a br
 oad range of study designs and approaches to analysis.\nHosted by Associat
 e Dean\, Academic\, Dr. Cheryl van Daalen-Smith\, RN\, PhD\nWebinar One: A
  Guide to Applied Qualitative Research\nThis webinar provides graduate stu
 dents\, supervisors\, and researchers with a practical foundation in appli
 ed qualitative research. Participants will explore key qualitative methodo
 logies\, research design considerations\, data collection strategies\, and
  approaches to generating rigorous and meaningful findings.\nWhen: Tuesday
 \, January 12\, 2027 from 11:00 a.m.-12:15 p.m.\nLocation: Zoom\n*Registra
 tion is required | RSVP Link\nWebinar Two: Coding Qualitative Data\nThis 
 webinar introduces the principles and practices of qualitative data coding
 \, from developing initial codes to identifying patterns and themes. Throu
 gh practical examples\, participants will learn strategies for organizing\
 , analyzing\, and interpreting qualitative data in a systematic and transp
 arent manner.\nWhen: Tuesday\, February 9\, 2027 from 11:00 a.m.-12:15 p.m
 .\nLocation: Zoom\n*Registration is required | RSVP Link\nWebinar Three: 
 Generative AI in Qualitative Data Analysis \nThis webinar examines the eme
 rging role of generative artificial intelligence (GenAI) in qualitative re
 search and data analysis. Participants will explore opportunities\, limita
 tions\, ethical considerations\, and practical applications of GenAI tools
  to support coding\, theme development\, data synthesis\, and research pro
 ductivity while maintaining methodological rigor.\nWhen: Tuesday\, March 9
 \, 2027 from 11:00 a.m.-12:15 p.m.\nLocation: Zoom\n*Registration is requi
 red | RSVP Link\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260818
LOCATION:Live on Zoom @ Zoom
ORGANIZER;CN="Faculty of Graduate Studies":MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/applied-qualitative-research/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
