BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Torontobotanicalgarden": "https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/floral-design-program-creative-design-4/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:torontobotanicalgarden
X-SOURCE:Toronto Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270112T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270202T210000
DTSTAMP:20261114T011902
CREATED:20261104T163911Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261104T163957Z
UID:10002046-1799776800-1801602000@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:Floral Design Program: Creative Design
DESCRIPTION:Creative Design builds on the skills and styles learned in Fundamentals I and II.\nYou’ll explore design styles\, such as Parallel\, Satellitic\, Synergistic\, Visible Use of Water\, and you’ll think outside the vase\, doing a Duo Design. This course explores a worldwide trend to move away from traditional rules of design towards freedom of expression.\n \nPrerequisites: Classic Design Fundamentals I & II.\n \nCourse fees do not include flowers or supplies. Students are encouraged to find a local flower shop or grocery store to purchase their flowers. A materials list will be emailed prior to the start of each class.\n \nLearn more about our Certificate in Floral Design\n \nTuesdays\, January 12\, 19\, 26 & February 2\, 6 to 9 p.m.\nPublic $245\, Members $195 (plus applicable taxes and fees)\n \nAbout Pat Ware\nPat has enjoyed teaching a number of different Floral Design courses at the Toronto Botanical Garden. She is a Design\, Horticultural and Rose Judge. Pat continues to participate in and learn about Floral Artistry at the local\, Provincial and international levels.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program\, please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/floral-design-program-creative-design-4/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Avenue East\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Floral Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/68ae016e7575160f927f3141fe3e99ed.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad8f041e9f71840dd72aea6"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:AI and Creativity: Can Technology Inspire the Human Imagination?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270112T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270112T190000
UID:6ad8f041e9f71840dd72aea6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This presentation explores the increasingly complicated relati
 onship between technology and creativity. Rather than treating AI as simpl
 y good or bad\, participants consider whether technology can generate crea
 tive sparks while examining the distinctly human elements of imagination\,
  subjective experience\, choice and authorship. Drawing on more than 30 ye
 ars in magazines\, writing and publishing presented by international award
  winning author Lisa de Nikolits.\nRegistration required.\nInformation Col
 lection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the
  Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 
 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program
  registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library h
 andles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline
 @tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad8f041e9f71840dd72aea6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
