ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 06/instructor-engagedsmallgroup-scaled.jpg
CATEGORIES:Graduate Program in Political Science,Teaching &amp\; Learning
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260629
DESCRIPTION:Throughout this course\, you will have the opportunity to prac
 tice and experience different instructional strategies with peers from acr
 oss the university. Discussion and reflection will centre around the ways 
 in which your instructional strategies are informed by the teaching and le
 arning literature\, and the ways you use the strategies intentionally to a
 lign with your teaching beliefs and commitments to Decolonizing\, Equity\,
  Diversity\, Inclusion\, and Accessibility (DEDIA).\nBy the end of the cou
 rse\, you will\n– Connect and learn collaboratively with a community of 
 individuals committed to professional development in teaching and learning
 \n– Investigate the ways in which teaching strategies are used intention
 ally\n– Express and practice different teaching and learning strategies 
 to design and teach a 10-minute BOPPPS lesson giving and receiving feedbac
 k based on DEDIA and research evidence\nPlease note that registration clos
 es on January 4\, 2027 at 11:59pm ET.\nThe course will consist of five 2-h
 our synchronous sessions spread between January 14 to March 18\, 2027 (det
 ails below) via Zoom. Online learning and preparation between sessions wil
 l be required\, for a total time commitment of approximately 20 hours.\nRe
 gister using our registration form ( https://yulearn.yorku.ca/local/yulear
 n/learning_opportunity.php?id=2262 ).\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261110
LOCATION:Online via Zoom.
ORGANIZER;CN="Teaching Commons":MAILTO:teaching@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/teaching-assistant-certificate-in-teach
 ing-tact-winter-2027-virtual-course/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
