SUMMARY:From Learning to Action: An Applied Learning Series for Future Soc
 ial Service & Allied Health Professionals
DTSTART:20270126T173000Z
DTEND:20270126T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261009T162800Z
UID:MEC-bfd685335fc8efd8ca3201f28dabe7a7@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20270126T173000Z
SEQUENCE:5
CATEGORIES:LA&amp\;PS School of Social Work
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261009
DESCRIPTION:Join us for this engaging five-part\, in-person learning exper
 ience for LA&PS students interested in social work\, health and community-
 based careers. Gain practical insights from experienced professionals into
  topics such as crisis response\, mental health\, housing\, immigration an
 d the justice system. Attend the session(s) that interest you most or atte
 nd all five to earn a Certificate of Completion. \nHosted by the School
  of the School of Social Work Field Education Office\, Community & Legal A
 id Services Program (CLASP)\, and Complex Communities. \nSession 3: Intro
 duction to Tenant Rights and the LTB in Ontario \nTuesday\, Jan. 26\, 202
 7 | 12:30 – 2 p.m. \nRegister Today\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261009
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/from-learning-to-action-an-applied-lear
 ning-series-for-future-social-service-health-professionals-424-608/
