BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/tea-time-talk-mental-health-matters/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Tea Time Talk: Mental Health Matters
DTSTART:20270127T170000Z
DTEND:20270127T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20261106T183500Z
UID:MEC-5242ef6f489fc9c35ba357927f91a59f@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20270127T170000Z
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:BE-YU,Bethune College,Calumet College,Colleges,Equity, Diversit
 y &amp\; Inclusion,Equity, People &amp\; Culture,Faculties,Faculty of Grad
 uate Studies (Programs),Faculty of Health,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp\; P
 rofessional Studies,Faculty of Science,Health Education &amp\; Promotion,L
 A&amp\;PS Colleges,LA&amp\;PS Community Hub,LA&amp\;PS Founders College,LA
 &amp\;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp\;PS New College,LA&amp\;PS Vanier Colle
 ge,Lassonde School of Engineering,Osgoode Hall Law School,School of Contin
 uing Studies,School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp\; Design,Stong Co
 llege,Student Accessibility Services,Student Counselling, Health &amp\; We
 ll-being,Students,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students,Th
 e Centre,Well-being
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261106
DESCRIPTION:Health is about more than how we feel physically. Join Student
  Counselling\, Health and Well-Being for a warm conversation exploring the
  six dimensions of well-being\, what mental health really means and how it
  supports us as students and in everyday life\, especially during the dark
 \, cold winter months.\nWe’ll talk about the winter blues and simple way
 s to care for your mental health\, then create your own Winter Wellness Ki
 t— a personalized set of tools and feel-good strategies to take home.\nG
 rab a cup of tea\, bring your questions and let’s talk about mental heal
 th in a way that feels real\, supportive and fun.\nLight refreshments prov
 ided\nOpen to all York University Students\nDate: Wednesday\, January 27th
 \, 2027\nTime: noon – 1:30 p.m.\nLocation: Founders College 305\nYou are
  welcome to drop in\, but registering helps us make sure there are enough 
 refreshments and supplies for everyone.\nRegister for Tea Time Talks: Ment
 al Health Matters\nThe Tea Time Talks is coordinated by the LA&PS Colleges
