CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Faculty of Graduate Studies (Progra
 ms),Glendon Maîtrise en affaires publiques et internationales (MAPI),Glen
 don Masters in Public &amp\; International Affairs,Graduate Diploma in Bio
 technology,Graduate Diploma in Management,Graduate Diploma in Neuroscience
 ,Graduate Diploma in Professional Accounting,Graduate Program in Administr
 ation,Graduate Program in Art History,Graduate Program in Biology,Graduate
  Program in Biotechnology Management,Graduate Program in Chemistry,Graduat
 e Program in Cinema &amp\; Media Studies,Graduate Program in Civil Enginee
 ring,Graduate Program in Communication and Culture,Graduate Program in Con
 ference Interpreting,Graduate Program in Critical Disability Studies,Gradu
 ate Program in Dance,Graduate Program in Design,Graduate Program in Develo
 pment Studies,Graduate Program in Digital Media,Graduate Program in Disast
 er &amp\; Emergency Management,Graduate Program in Earth &amp\; Space Scie
 nce,Graduate Program in Economics,Graduate Program in Education,Graduate P
 rogram in Education–Leadership &amp\; Community Engagement,Graduate Prog
 ram in Electrical Engineering &amp\; Computer Science,Graduate Program in 
 English,Graduate Program in Environmental Studies,Graduate Program in Film
 ,Graduate Program in Financial Accountability,Graduate Program in French a
 nd Francophone Studies,Graduate Program in Gender, Feminist and Women's St
 udies,Graduate Program in Geography,Graduate Program in Global Health,Grad
 uate Program in Health,Graduate Program in History,Graduate Program in Hum
 an Resources Management,Graduate Program in Humanities,Graduate Program in
  Information Systems &amp\; Technology,Graduate Program in Interdisciplina
 ry Studies,Graduate Program in Kinesiology and Health Science,Graduate Pro
 gram in Law,Graduate Program in Linguistics &amp\; Applied Linguistics,Gra
 duate Program in Management Practice,Graduate Program in Mathematics &amp\
 ; Statistics,Graduate Program in Mechanical Engineering,Graduate Program i
 n Music,Graduate Program in Nursing,Graduate Program in Philosophy,Graduat
 e Program in Physics &amp\; Astronomy,Graduate Program in Political Scienc
 e,Graduate Program in Psychology,Graduate Program in Public Policy, Admini
 stration and Law,Graduate Program in Science &amp\; Technology Studies,Gra
 duate Program in Social &amp\; Political Thought,Graduate Program in Socia
 l Anthrolology,Graduate Program in Social Work,Graduate Program in Socio-L
 egal Studies,Graduate Program in Sociology,Graduate Program in Theatre,Gra
 duate Program in Theatre, Dance &amp\; Performance Studies,Graduate Progra
 m in Translation Studies,Graduate Program in Visual Art,LA&amp\;PS Student
 s-Graduate,Markham Campus
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260928
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies is hosting a session entitled 
 Digital Research Tools for Doctoral Success. Join us!\nDoctoral research i
 nvolves managing complex projects\, vast amounts of information\, and evol
 ving workflows. The right digital tools can help researchers work more eff
 iciently\, stay organized\, and make the research process more manageable.
  This session explores practical tools and strategies for citation managem
 ent\, note-taking\, collaboration\, writing\, project planning\, and organ
 izing your research workflow. Participants will learn how digital approach
 es can support effective research practices and help develop sustainable s
 ystems for navigating the demands of advanced scholarship.\nDate: Wednesda
 y\, February 3\, 2027\nTime: 12:00-1:00 p.m. (ET)\nLocation: Virtual Works
 hop via Zoom Webinar\nRegistration is required: Registration Form ( https:
 //yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_YqxllMC-SZuq55Q6grgDag )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261005
LOCATION:Online Zoom Webinar @ Online Zoom Webinar
ORGANIZER;CN="Faculty of Graduate Studies":MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/fgs-event-digital-research-tools-februa
 ry-3/
