BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aeb7d51035faf0033e15f83"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Excel Basics 2: Do More with your Data
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20270208T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20270208T150000
UID:6aeb7d51035faf0033e15f83@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on Microsoft Excel for beginners with li
 ttle or no Excel experience. Build on your basic Microsoft Excel skills an
 d learn to use Excel data effectively.\nIn this second session\, you will:
 \nPractice data entry and formatting\nManipulate rows and columns\nCreate 
 and copy simple formulas\nConvert data to a Table then sort and filter\nCr
 eate your first chart\nUpon completion of this class\, you will be able to
  get more from your data using tables\, filters and charts.\nPrerequisites
 : Excel Basics Part 1 or equivalent knowledge. Basic mouse and keyboard sk
 ills required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information o
 n this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Li
 braries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will onl
 y be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Qu
 estions about how the library handles your information can be directed to 
 Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Cliffcrest
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aeb7d51035faf0033e15f83
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/beyond-the-academy-2027/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Beyond the Academy 2027
DTSTART:20270208T150000Z
DTEND:20270208T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20261110T165800Z
UID:MEC-435c53251dc1f41d8d6b80f8592f6650@events.yorku.ca__20270208
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:LA&amp\;PS Colleges,LA&amp\;PS Students-Graduate
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261110
DESCRIPTION:Beyond the Academy is a five-week applied professional develop
 ment program designed to help LA&PS PhD students:\n• Understand the land
 scape of non-academic careers.\n• Reflect on personal values and strengt
 hs.\n• Translate academic experience into professional competencies.\n
 • Build professional networks and online presence.\n• Develop concrete
  strategies for career exploration and job searching.\nThe program will be
  cohort-based\, combining reflective exercises\, practical workshops\, and
  alumni engagement. It will culminate in an actionable career plan and pro
 fessional online profile for each participant.\nTo apply to the program\, 
 please complete the required registration form:\nBeyond the Academy Regist
 ration Form\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261110
ORGANIZER;CN="Marco Sestito":MAILTO:msestito@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/beyond-the-academy-2027/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
