CATEGORIES:Equity, Diversity &amp\; Inclusion,Equity, People &amp\; Cultur
 e
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260923
DESCRIPTION:This session will follow the birth and development of anti-Bla
 ck racism both globally and locally\, and the historic and on-going effort
 s to dismantle it. Through case-studies and scenarios\, participants will 
 be offered tools and examples of how to respond to anti-Black racism in ef
 fective and sustainable ways.\n
