BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/virtual-drop-in-session-master-of-biotechnology-management-mbm-graduate-diploma-in-biotechnology-gdb-3/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Virtual Drop-In Session: Master of Biotechnology Management (MBM) 
 & Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology (GDB)
DTSTART:20270211T153000Z
DTEND:20270211T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260721T141200Z
UID:MEC-cd6c652e6f498d4363bff3c4b63bd685@events.yorku.ca__20270211
SEQUENCE:4
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology,G
 raduate Program in Biotechnology Management
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260721
DESCRIPTION:The Master of Biotechnology Management  is a course- and 
 experiential learning-based graduate program designed for students who 
 hold a bachelor of science degree in biology\, biological sciences\, bio
 technology\, life science\, or related discipline\, and have little/no wor
 k experience in biotechnology. It provides practical interdisciplinary tra
 ining in biotechnology and management to enhance student competitiveness
  and employability in the biotechnology sector. Graduates from this prog
 ram are prepared to contribute to the sector in roles that require scient
 ific\, technical\, and management skills and competencies.  \nThe Grad
 uate Diploma in Biotechnology is a graduate certification for students w
 ho hold a bachelor of science degree in biology\, biological sciences\, 
 biotechnology\, life science\, or related discipline\, and have little/no 
 work experience in biotechnology. It provides scientific and technical 
 training in biotechnology to enhance graduate competitiveness and emplo
 yability in the biotechnology sector. Students acquire the skills and c
 ompetencies required to address labour gaps in the biotechnology sector
  and strengthen the Canadian economy. \nDrop by one of our virtual sessio
 ns on Thursdays from 11:30 a.m. to 12:00 p.m. to meet the graduate pr
 ogram director and graduate program administrator who will be able to answ
 er questions about the programs. \nRegister in advance for this meeting:\
 nMeeting Registration – Zoom\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260930
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/virtual-drop-in-session-master-of-biote
 chnology-management-mbm-graduate-diploma-in-biotechnology-gdb-3/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/common-hour-oscar-peterson-jazz-artist-in-residence-featuring-guitarist-rez-abbasi/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Common Hour: Oscar Peterson Jazz Artist-in-Residence featuring gui
 tarist Rez Abbasi
DTSTART:20270211T173000Z
DTEND:20270211T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260928T152700Z
UID:MEC-1b80bd6703c274cdb50d8d1fd2a020ab@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20270211T173000Z
SEQUENCE:1
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 09/res.jpg
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp\; Design
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260928
DESCRIPTION:The Oscar Peterson Jazz Artist-in-Residence program at York Un
 iversity brings renowned jazz musicians to the Department of Music each ye
 ar for multi-day residencies featuring student workshops\, masterclasses\,
  and a culminating public performance.\nAward winning guitarist\, Rez Abba
 si ( https://www.reztone.com/ ) is featured as part of the Department of M
 usic’s 2026-2027 Oscar Peterson Jazz Artist-in-Residence.\nThe following
  session is free and open to the public.\nDate: Thursday\, February 11\nTi
 me: 12:30 – 1:30 p.m.\nLocation: Tribute Communities Recital Hall\nFree 
 Admission\nREZ ABBASI\nGuitarist\, composer\, author and 2021 Guggenheim F
 ellow\, Rez Abbasi is among a rare\nbreed of artists that continue to push
  boundaries from within the traditions he has\nembraced. Consistently plac
 ing on DownBeat magazine’s International Critics Poll in\nGuitar alongsi
 de luminaries Bill Frisell and Pat Metheny since 2014\, Abbasi continues t
 o\nforge new ground with his multi-dimensional projects.\n“Abbasi is liv
 ing\, breathing proof that jazz music can be as vital and boundary-pushing
  as\never.” AllAboutJazz.com.\nBorn in Karachi\, Pakistan\, migrating to
  Southern California at the age of four\, schooled\nat the University of S
 outhern California and the Manhattan School of Music in jazz and\nclassica
 l music\, along with a pilgrimage in India under the guidance of master\np
 ercussionist\, Ustad Alla Rakha\, Abbasi is a vivid synthesis of all the a
 bove stated\ninfluences and genres.\n“Mr. Abbasi succeeded in making som
 e fairly cerebral intricacies feel intuitive and\ntouched by a higher purp
 ose.” – New York Times\nThe Oscar Peterson Jazz Artist-in-Residence is
  made possible by a grant from the Ministry of Training\, Colleges and Uni
 versities.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260928
LOCATION:Tribute Communities Recital Hall Accolade East Building\, York Un
 iversity @ 4700 Keele Street
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/common-hour-oscar-peterson-jazz-artist-
 in-residence-featuring-guitarist-rez-abbasi/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
